  ["Greetings, $c. If you're looking for training, you'll need to find a $c trainer. I only instruct rogues."]=1,
},
[168619]={ -- Huinli Wingpaw
  ["Greetings, $c. If you're looking for training, you'll need to find a $c trainer. I only instruct monks."]=1,
},
[168621]={ -- Martin Goodchilde
  ["Greetings, $c. If you're looking for training, you'll need to find a $c trainer. I only instruct priests."]=1,
},
[168623]={ -- Kazak Darkscream
  ["Greetings, $c. If you're looking for training, you'll need to find a $c trainer. I only instruct warlocks."]=1,
},
[168626]={ -- Feenix Arcshine
  ["Greetings, $c. Have you come to learn about combat specializations?"]=1,
  ["Greetings, $c. If you're looking for training, you'll need to find a $c trainer. I only instruct mages."]=2,
},
[168628]={ -- Hretar Riverspeaker
  ["Greetings, $c. If you're looking for training, you'll need to find a $c trainer. I only instruct shaman."]=1,
},
[169718]={ -- Veteran Crusader Aliocha Segard
  ["How may I help you?"]=1,
},
[169999]={ -- Spirit Obelisk
  ["It is not yet your time. I shall aid your journey back to the realm of the living... for a price."]=1,
},
[171689]={ -- Nathoka Bloodfang
  ["You've come for training in order to pass it on to your pets?"]=1,
  ["Ah friend, I only help hunters and their pets."]=2,
},
[171791]={ -- Nazgrim
  ["The Ebon Blade stands ready."]=1,
  ["Much has happened in your absence, $c. Let me catch you up to speed."]=2,
  ["Mograine asked that I stay behind in case you strayed too far off course. This death gate will take you to him. I suggest you use it."]=3,
},
[171808]={ -- Ta'tru
  ["Welcome. Are you buying or selling today?"]=1,
},
[172558]={ -- Eyla Pathleader
  ["Hello there, $c. I offer ways for seasoned travelers to aid others they meet along the way."]=1,
},
[172572]={ -- Celeste Periwinkle
  ["Hello there, $c. I offer ways for seasoned travelers to aid others they meet along the way."]=1,
},
[173057]={ -- Steward Caterer
  ["Want drink? Very tasty!"]=1,
  ["Aspirant is thirsty? Steward has drink!"]=2,
  ["<The steward offers you his tray with a soft hoot.>"]=3,
  ["Hoo! This one has drink! Take! Take!"]=4,
},
[173257]={ -- Caregiver Maximillian
  ["I have waited dozens of years for a worthy opponent. To the victor go the spoils!"]=1,
},
[173350]={ -- Ba'vol
  ["Welcome, Maw Walker. This device will allow you to access shard storage from across the dimensions that separate this world from yours. Unlike our Attendant friends over there, with their hallowed Purpose, I understand how it functions. I will not tell you how though. Consider it a trade secret. You are however free to use it. Compliments of the Brokers."]=1,
},
[173357]={ -- Keeper Ta'hilt
  ["Welcome, Maw Walker. Not everything you see is for sale. We also collect. Such curious creatures we have found in your realm. I am enjoying expanding my collection."]=1,
},
[173365]={ -- Contemplative Scribe
  ["I wonder where these changes will lead. The Purpose has always guided us. That suggests this is still the Purpose. I just do not know how this will end. Even a small cog wants to understand the meaning of their role."]=1,
  ["The Purpose can provide a wonderfully contemplative view now and again, can't it?"]=2,
  ["We all have a part to play. That is what the Purpose tells us. When we knew the meaning of our parts that was easy to believe. Now? I am not so sure. We must keep faith I guess. Trust in the Purpose. Our way is the Purpose."]=3,
  ["The Maw roils with such power, yet it is not in service of the Purpose. That is how the Purpose is testing us."]=4,
  ["This is such a beautiful view. Even as the Maw denies the Purpose, it is still an interlocking part of this realm."]=5,
  ["Our part in the Purpose cannot be determined with certainty at the moment. You may be used to this state, Maw Walker, but this is a very new feeling for us."]=6,
},
[173571]={ -- Photonic Gearhaggle
  ["Good day, adventurer. If you require my services as an auctioneer, I regret to inform you: no. Only grand master engineers possess the minimum intellectual capacity to interface with my superior functions.$b$bMore importantly, why are you still talking to me?"]=1,
  ["Hello, adventurer. My services as an auctioneer are available to those with skill in engineering. Sadly, you have none. Please leave."]=2,
},
[173705]={ -- Archivist Janeera
  ["<Archivist Janeera doesn't make eye contact with you as she continues to read the scroll in front of her.> Yes?"]=1,
},
[173819]={ -- Reckful
  ["I don't train Assassination Rogues."]=1,
},
[173998]={ -- Crusader Olakin Sainrith
  ["The Scourge must be stopped at any cost. We cannot permit them to field the army they're constructing here."]=1,
},
[174035]={ -- Dro Seminario
  ["The bass needs to be tighter. The kick needs to be punchier. You call this a venue? It's a cave! There's no warmth, and the acoustics are shoddy at best. Blight Boar can't go live until this sounds perfect. Just because I'm undead doesn't mean my ears aren't finely tuned!"]=1,
},
[174146]={ -- Archivist Thomas
  ["Do you wish to hear a tale from the past, adventurer?"]=1,
},
[174564]={ -- Caretaker Kah-Rahm
  ["This area provides you access to services relating to your material possessions. We are relatively new to such concepts, so the Brokers have kindly offered to facilitate these services for you."]=1,
},
[174766]={ -- Cortinarius
  ["Welcome to The Ring, friend. Some say this is the center of Ardenweald, or where Marasmius first grew. Only he knows for sure."]=1,
  ["The Ring used to be a way station of sorts, a hub where you could travel almost anywhere in Ardenweald. $b$BWith the passage of time and the recent drought, even Marasmius has lost some of his paths. Perhaps with enough anima the damage can be reversed...$b$bFor now, it is the duty of the mushroomancers to tend to Marasmius. We will rebuild Ardenweald's roots stronger than before, and we will ensure its survival."]=2,
  ["Honorary mushroomancer, eh? Marasmius really seems to have taken a shine to you. Welcome to the team!$B$BUh, it was just me before. But I'm glad you're here now! As part of your mushroomancer duties you will have access to the paths of Marasmius. You also get access to a number of exciting perks and mushroomancer-exclusive equipment. As you help me and Marasmius you'll earn tokens that I can exchange for you."]=3,
},
[174794]={ -- Kyrian Steward
  ["Hoo! Hello! New aspirant! Yay!"]=1,
  ["Hi! You new! Very good! Yes!"]=2,
  ["AHH! New aspirant! Ring bells! Sound horns! Best day!!!"]=3,
  ["Make clean. Make nice. Bastion beautiful, yes?"]=4,
  ["You want, I get?"]=5,
  ["<The steward hums a jolly tune to himself.>"]=6,
  ["We help! What do you need?"]=7,
  ["I get you something?"]=8,
},
[175135]={ -- Rokhan
  ["Da Horde be facin' many trials. Many dangers. I'm proud ta be a voice on da council dat's gonna lead us forward. Vol'jin was da finest warchief we ever knew... and a good friend. I can only hope ta be honorin' his memory by never lettin' da Horde forget da sacrifices he made for us."]=1,
},
[175137]={ -- High Exarch Turalyon
  ["In King Anduin's absence, I have been entrusted with the protection of Alliance citizens. It feels like lifetimes ago that I helped a young Varian Wrynn secure his throne. Now I am charged with keeping it safe for his son. The Fourth War took a terrible toll on the Alliance. Our military might has been depleted. Stormwind's nobles are keen to see our defenses restored. Reclaiming Stromgarde was a good first step. Perhaps there are other holdings of the old Alliance that could be secured."]=1,
},
[175138]={ -- Alleria Windrunner
  ["We spent months searching every inch of Azeroth for any sign of Sylvanas, only to learn that my sister has crossed into the realms of the dead. <Alleria's eyes narrow.> How fitting. Though I long to join the hunt for her, right now my place is here. The Alliance must rebuild its strength, and I will aid Turalyon in that effort. But when the time comes, I will see Sylvanas answer for what she had done."]=1,
},
[176650]={ -- Vigilant Defender
  ["Blessings of the Naaru. What can I help you find?"]=1,
},
[177193]={ -- Kiku
  ["Looking to hear a story?"]=1,
},
[177208]={ -- Eppu
  ["Looking to hear a story?"]=1,
},
[178792]={ -- Ta'meri
  ["Do you need something shipped?"]=1,
},
[178804]={ -- Ta'hsup
  ["Welcome, friend. Have you any interest in Keystones?"]=1,
},
[179144]={ -- Zo'mezal
  ["Halt. Only citizens and registered clients are allowed through this entrance."]=1,
},
[181097]={ -- Simon Sezdans
  ["You there! You look like you've cut a rug in your time. Do you think you've got what it takes to become a Dance Master? Grab your token and test your skills!"]=1,
},
[182082]={ -- Agapanthus
  ["If you intend no harm to my charges, you are welcome here, Traveler."]=1,
},
[183997]={ -- Gnoll Mon-Ark
  ["<The gnoll constantly adjusts a paper crown on their head.> Me first gnoll Mon-Ark. Gnolls dumb. Not obey crown! Need teach them. You help me, I no eat you. Fair, meat?"]=1,
  ["You make okay gnoll."]=2,
  ["You make okay gnoll, but better friend. <They look over your shoulder.> Other friends hungry though. Run!"]=3,
},
[184239]={ -- Hipponius
  ["I can deliver Anima for you back to Bastion, if you wish."]=1,
},
[184240]={ -- Aliotha
  ["I can deliver Anima for you back to Ardenweald, if you wish."]=1,
},
[184241]={ -- Brakka Noct
  ["I can deliver Anima for you back to Maldraxxus, if you desire."]=1,
},
[184242]={ -- Edwardi
  ["I can deliver Anima for you back to Revendreth, if you desire."]=1,
},
[185467]={ -- Wilder Seabraid
  ["Welcome to T&W Trading Post!"]=1,
},
[185468]={ -- Tawny Seabraid
  ["Welcome to T&W Trading Post!"]=1,
},
[185749]={ -- Gnoll Mon-Ark
  ["<The gnoll constantly adjusts a paper crown on their head.> Me first gnoll Mon-Ark. Gnolls dumb. Not obey crown! Need teach them. You help me, I no eat you. Fair, meat?"]=1,
  ["You make okay gnoll."]=2,
  ["You make okay gnoll, but better friend. <They look over your shoulder.> Other friends hungry though. Run!"]=3,
},
[185843]={ -- Ancient Console
  ["Return to Domination's Grasp?"]=1,
},
[186443]={ -- Skygazer Paatu
  ["Where would you like to fly?"]=1,
},
[187412]={ -- Happy Hal
  ["It's good to see you, friend. Take off your shoes and enjoy the fire before you set off on your grand adventures."]=1,
},
[187669]={ -- Nozdormu
  ["It is time we speak, adventurer."]=1,
},
[188046]={ -- Sindragosa
  ["Are you ready to leave the vault?"]=1,
},
[188054]={ -- Azure Guardian
  ["Are you lost, dracthyr?"]=1,
},
[188377]={ -- So'turu
  ["<So'turu gazes intensely at the coin in your hand.> Maw Walker! Have you come to trade? Allow us to show you the finest wares in all the Shadowlands."]=1,
},
[188904]={ -- John Stelle III
  ["I came on the first boat. (Couldn't even think about waiting, really.) We're the first to land in this place. Let that sink in a second. We're making history, adventurer!"]=1,
},
[189076]={ -- Pathfinder Jeb
  ["Everyone needs a little nudge now and again. They'll get it eventually. Wouldn't want to help 'em too much. The struggle is good for 'em!"]=1,
},
[189077]={ -- Toddy Whiskers
  ["Our scouts report that turbulent elemental storms are churning the seas to dangerous, unnatural levels. Until those clear, we won't be going anywhere. Why don't ye see what ye can help with around here while we wait?"]=1,
},
[189079]={ -- Thaelin Darkanvil
  ["This craftsmanship is somethin' else. Ye can learn a lot by studyin' the work of others. Just the thought of what lies ahead gets me excited!"]=1,
},
[189080]={ -- Cataloger Wulferd
  ["So many wondrous creatures! Fish! Birds! Oh, look up there! In the sky! It's a... YUCK! Not again! Why do they always do that right when I look up? Dampen a cloth in that beautiful ocean water, would you?"]=1,
},
[189479]={ -- Rumiastrasza
  ["Welcome to The Ruby Feast! Chef Morsel and I, the most stunning culinary duo in all the Isles, have prepared and laid out a most various array of flavorful delights! Dig in, dance, and enjoy the festivities!"]=1,
},
[189569]={ -- Wrathion
  ["Ah, there you are, adventurer. Impeccable timing! I briefed Lord Commander Turalyon on recent events, and have extended the Aspects' invitation to the Dragon Isles. We just have a few more details to discuss."]=1,
  ["There is so much for us to discuss. In time, the answers will come. You have my word."]=2,
},
[189600]={ -- High Exarch Turalyon
  ["The Aspects have been steadfast allies to Stormwind in the past. But enemies have arisen from among the dragons as well. Enemies that nearly destroyed this world. We must be cautious."]=1,
},
[189603]={ -- Scalecommander Azurathel
  ["I am Azurathel, commander of the Obsidian Warders. Wrathion guided us to this city to meet with your Alliance leaders. We are dracthyr, soldiers trained to fight for dragonkind. But we have been sealed away on distant shores for many an age, and your world is new to us. I do not yet know if your kind will prove worthy of our trust. But it seems we share a common foe, and perhaps through battle we will forge a bond between us."]=1,
},
[189763]={ -- Pathfinder Jeb
  ["Help ya with something? I'm sorta busy showing these trainees the finer points of scaling walls."]=1,
},
[189765]={ -- Cataloger Wulferd
  ["No quill? No ink? <The gnome shakes his head.> How do you expect me to sign an autograph if you don't come prepared?"]=1,
},
[189767]={ -- Thaelin Darkanvil
  ["This craftsmanship is somethin' else. Ye can learn a lot by studyin' the work of others. Just the thought of what lies ahead gets me excited!"]=1,
},
[189869]={ -- Valdrakken Citizen
  ["Welcome to Valdrakken, dracthyr!"]=1,
},
[189895]={ -- Valdrakken Citizen
  ["Who maintained these isles over the eons? We did! And what do we get for it? Nothing!"]=1,
  ["Hello, friend. Did you also get turned out of your home by the return of the 'masters'?"]=2,
},
[189952]={ -- Custodian Cynegos
  ["We have been spread thin these past ten thousand years. Ruins crumble. Books disintegrate. All of the recent developments in the isles have made our task more important than ever! These Kirin Tor mages have been particularly helpful in securing our ancient spaces, even if their apprentices are somewhat... excitable."]=1,
},
[190575]={ -- Cariel Roame
  ["Delivering justice can be quite the heavy task. But it is mine to carry."]=1,
},
[191150]={ -- Danielle Anglers
  ["Just imagine the kind of fish we might find here! Dragon fish! Proto-dragon fish! Or better yet--forbidden fish the dragons have been hiding away for centuries!"]=1,
},
[191205]={ -- Hemet Nesingwary
  ["You didn't think retirement would keep me out of the game, did you? My eyes aren't what they used to be, and my hands are certainly less steady... but they can hold these reins! This whole Dragonscale Expedition is quite the operation, and I've a mind to do my part! As for the Azure Span, well... it reminds me of some of the best places I've ever been."]=1,
  ["I've bagged enough trophies to last me ten lifetimes! Take Tiny and Junior here... Sure, I could put their heads on a wall as easy as pulling a pint of Dun Morogh stout, but it'd make my job as a wagon driver significantly harder! <Nesingwary laughs.> I suppose that makes me something of a conservationist!"]=2,
},
[191263]={ -- Salukan
  ["Where would you like to fly?"]=1,
},
[192926]={ -- Trainer Frodrum
  ["Have you come to prove your prowess to the Shikaar?"]=1,
},
[193015]={ -- Unatos
  ["Welcome, friend. How can we help you? The Valdrakken Accord is pleased to see the dracthyr return to the Reach. The dragons are expanding their influence again, and they spread their wings wide. I just hope we can piece together the mysteries of the dracthyr's past."]=1,
},
[193450]={ -- Archmage Khadgar
  ["We have much to discuss."]=1,
},
[194393]={ -- Clovis
  ["Oh, uh, hello. Name's Clovis. My job 'ere is holdin' the captain's rum, and runnin' downstairs tae get more of it when he runs dry. Somehow pays more'n the Ashvane Company ever did though."]=1,
},
[194397]={ -- Nethandril Duskthorn
  ["The Dragon Isles... An ancient land unknown to mere mortals, shrouded in grand secrecy. So much forgotten knowledge and obscure power now prime for the taking... Can you taste it already, $r? I can."]=1,
},
[194484]={ -- Clinkora Rustfuse
  ["This is terrible! I thought we were taking an airship! I never bought the advanced anti-moisture circuitry upgrades! I'm done for!"]=1,
},
[194488]={ -- Guldros Onyxbrand
  ["Oh! By the flames, keep the water offa me! Me dad got extinguished once. We had ta kindle him twice a day fer a month before he could walk straight again! These dragons better be worth it!"]=1,
},
[194490]={ -- Zuraan
  ["Oh, by the Light-- How do they stand the constant rocking? I will never board a vessel without auto-balancing calibrator arrays again."]=1,
},
[194493]={ -- Ogdan Stoneforge
  ["Ye know, a lotta dwarves won't set foot on a boat. We're dense an' heavy, and they're afraid they'd sink straight tae the bottom if they went overboard. Not me though. I like tae feel the sea breeze in me moustache."]=1,
},
[194536]={ -- Reluun
  ["Light willing, Tishad will be eaten by a dragon within a few days. Only then will I know peace."]=1,
},
[194537]={ -- Tishad
  ["Ah, just like old times. Reluun and I were roommates on the Genedar. We have been best friends ever since. Let us hope this voyage is a bit shorter than that one though."]=1,
},
[194538]={ -- Ji-Min Quickpaw
  ["Oh, think of how jealous the cloud serpent riders will be when I come back to Pandaria with a real dragon friend!"]=1,
},
[194539]={ -- Tizzi Twistcog
  ["Exciting news! I received funding from the workshop to finish my research in the Dragon Isles! I'm working on electrothermal structures and their impact on arclight magnophoresis in environments with and without quasi-temporal samophlangic resonance. Rudimentary principles certainly, but just think of the applications!"]=1,
},
[194602]={ -- Book of Translocation
  ["The runes in this book suggest it can take you to the top ring within the Crystal Chambers."]=1,
},
[194613]={ -- Unkimi
  ["I like to gaze out over the wide open expanse of the span below as it stretches towards Iskaara, severed by the serpentine flow of the river. I like to hear the water's roar."]=1,
},
[194712]={ -- Book of Translocation
  ["The runes in this book suggest it can take you to the middle ring within the Crystal Chambers."]=1,
},
[194713]={ -- Book of Translocation
  ["The runes in this book suggest it can take you to the Mausoleum of Legends Entrance."]=1,
},
[194714]={ -- Book of Translocation
  ["The runes in this book suggest it can take you to the bottom ring within the Crystal Chambers."]=1,
},
[194715]={ -- Book of Translocation
  ["The runes in this book suggest it can take you to Sindragosa's Lament."]=1,
},
[195524]={ -- Beastmaster Tirren
  ["I tend to our beasts of burden."]=1,
},
[195540]={ -- Basran
  ["<You extend a hand to offer Basran pets, but he stays stoically next to his khan. Basran is currently working and you should not pet service dogs on duty.>"]=1,
},
[195545]={ -- Okir
  ["Please direct your attention to my khan."]=1,
  ["My khan is deaf, communicating mainly through a sign language that is shared amongst the centaur. I am but her voice, interpreting for her. While most members of our clan can speak with her without my aid, there are still many who cannot. My role is to enable communication between her and others. It is the highest honor. My words are hers. Except these ones. Please direct your attention back to her."]=2,
  ["Ah, Basran. He is a very good bakar, trained specifically to be Sansok Khan's ears. He alerts her for many sounds in different ways, working as an extension of her senses. While on a hunt, Basran supports Sansok Khan by signaling the direction and intensity of different environmental cues to her. He also looks out for anything that needs her attention, from a clanmate's shout to the drumming of hooves to the whistle of an approaching storm. Sansok Khan trains her hearing dogs herself, and has done so since a very young age. In fact, Basran is her third bakar, the son of her first!"]=3,
},
[195606]={ -- Beastmaster Zira
  ["I've never met a beast I couldn't win over. I've worked with rockfangs, hornstriders, even thunder lizards! But no animal can beat a bakar in loyalty and honor."]=1,
},
[195680]={ -- Playful Whelp
  ["<The whelp stares off into the distance, muttering under their breath.> Are they gonna be home for dinner?"]=1,
},
[195683]={ -- Studious Whelp
  ["Volcanoes have pipes under them where lava goes!"]=1,
  ["If I met a gnoll, I would poke him with a stick. <The whelp nods matter-of-factly.>"]=2,
  ["Sometimes people find a lot of gold and silver in rocks!"]=3,
},
[196087]={ -- Quartermaster Ashu
  ["Many different clans full of many different centaur bringing many different supplies... It is almost impossible to coordinate everything, but we do the best that we can."]=1,
},
[196091]={ -- Korston Willard
  ["For the better part of two decades, I've worked for the Night Watch in Duskwood. It was a hard job on the best days. On the worst ones... well, I've taken a lot of funeral leave in those twenty years... I put in my resignation last week. It's good to feel the sun again."]=1,
},
[196154]={ -- Rok
  ["Keep moving, void elf."]=1,
},
[196449]={ -- Elder Odgerel
  ["Clan Teerai are the proud protectors of tradition and good values. This meeting at Maruukai is also our tradition."]=1,
},
[196707]={ -- Quartermaster Huseng
  ["Good trade follows trust."]=1,
},
[196725]={ -- Chef Sungshin Ironpaw
  ["Welcome, fellow traveler. I am Chef Sungshin Ironpaw, Guide to the Ways and administrant to the Halfhill Market. A curious letter made it's way to me in the Valley of the Four Winds, written by Chef Morsel. He informed me that these Isles had opened and that he and his partner would be hosting a garden party of sorts. They would use it as an opportunity to showcase the rare ingredients of the Dragon Isles, as well as the wide variety of cuisines Azeroth has to offer. I simply couldn't refuse a request to exhibit the wonders of our great Pandaria! Please feel free to try my own offerings. We Pandaren are always on the move, so we've found food that travels with you is always the most satisfying."]=1,
},
[196974]={ -- Black Dragonflight Recruiter
  ["Welcome to Algeth'ar Academy! You look like you would make a powerful Black Dragonflight pledge. What do you think? Are you strong enough?"]=1,
},
[196977]={ -- Bronze Dragonflight Recruiter
  ["Well, you have arrived just in time to pledge the Bronze Dragonflight. Don't let this moment pass you by!"]=1,
},
[196978]={ -- Blue Dragonflight Recruiter
  ["Hello fellow student! Did you know that the Blue Dragonflight has maintained the highest grade point average of all the flights? If you can't wait to hit the books, pledge to the Blue Dragonflight!"]=1,
},
[196979]={ -- Green Dragonflight Recruiter
  ["Woah friend, slow down and relax a second with me. Find out why the Green Dragonflight is the absolute complete best and why you should totally pledge with us. Do you know how to throw a dragon disc?"]=1,
},
[196981]={ -- Red Dragonflight Recruiter
  ["Welcome new students, I know you must be so excited for the coming year! You should really think about pledging to the Red Dragonflight, we are going to have the best parties."]=1,
},
[197081]={ -- Sindragosa
  ["You've opened arcane pathways within the vault. Where would you like to go?"]=1,
},
[197711]={ -- Lindormi
  ["Tales of adventure are the best! Dark dungeons, terrifying monsters, shiny treasures... I want to hear all about them! If you promise to bring back a good story, I might even let you borrow a keystone."]=1,
},
[197766]={ -- Attentive Whelp
  ["<The whelp stares at the storyteller in awe.>"]=1,
},
[197792]={ -- Banshi
  ["I go where da food be."]=1,
},
[198079]={ -- Chrovo
  ["Are you looking to travel to the Dragon Isles? The Rugged Dragonscale can get you there in no time."]=1,
},
[198146]={ -- Liza Breezewood
  ["Heading back to Stormwind, are ya? Give my best to Chrovo when you arrive on the docks."]=1,
},
[198156]={ -- Brackenhide Announcer
  ["You put on good show, meat."]=1,
},
[198401]={ -- Dervishian
  ["Welcome to our makeshift training ring, friend. I trust we are not disturbing anyone up here? I've instructed the warders to be very careful to keep blasts of magic from falling down below."]=1,
},
[198446]={ -- Storidormi
  ["Hello, traveller! Have you come to hear a tale? Take a seat, and I'll tell you a story."]=1,
},
[198526]={ -- Nirathan
  ["We dracthyr are used to the wide-open spaces of the Reach, not the narrow confines of a city. Every street looks the same! An aerial view would make navigation easier. But I am determined to find my way around Stormwind the way the humans do. Life must be so hard without wings..."]=1,
},
[198531]={ -- Zaralash
  ["These guards fail to comprehend the inadequacies of this city's aerial defenses. They claim their gryphon riders are expertly trained, but I easily outflanked them. Then the riders complained that I spooked their gryphons, as if it was my fault they hadn't noticed my approach! I am told there is a war room in Stormwind Keep. I will go there at once and make certain this serious defensive oversight is addressed!"]=1,
},
[198532]={ -- Zhakloskar
  ["This city is truly a wonder. And its inhabitants have--for the most part--been quite welcoming. One even offered me a book. I assumed it would be a training manual, but instead it is a work of fiction describing the adventures of a character named Marcus. We dracthyr were trained to be soldiers, and were given very little free time to pursue reading for the sake of enjoyment. But I like this book. Perhaps I may even try my hand at writing a story of my own!"]=1,
},
[198533]={ -- Nazurathar
  ["To better blend in with the civilian population, I purchased this decorative helm from a local shopkeep. Though the craftsmanship is fine, I fear I must question its value. This helm offers little protection, though I am told I should be appreciative of something known as 'fashion appeal.'"]=1,
},
[198551]={ -- Thaza
  ["I wish to recruit some fellow adventurers to join me on an expedition, but none of us can agree on where to go. Is this sort of indecision common? I confess, I'm used to simply following my scalecommander's orders."]=1,
},
[198579]={ -- Valarian
  ["Almost every month new and exotic creatures arrive in the Trading Post. When we have creatures to trade you can see the Seabraids offerings right here."]=1,
},
[198581]={ -- Sam Corff
  ["Sorry, I'm busy stocking. You want to talk to the Seabraids."]=1,
},
[198589]={ -- Assistant Dilya
  ["Every month we get new outfits and weapons from all over. It's my job to make sure these outfits and weapons are properly displayed."]=1,
},
[198883]={ -- Vanessa VanCleef
  ["Stay out of my way, 'hero'."]=1,
},
[198895]={ -- Alregosa
  ["I am sorry $c, but my lessons are not for you."]=1,
},
[198896]={ -- Master Mathias Shaw
  ["Keep your wits about you."]=1,
},
[199923]={ -- Senegos
  ["I appreciate your patience, adventurer. I'm sure we'll get this place cleaned in no time."]=1,
},
[200099]={ -- Stellagosa
  ["It's fascinating to be standing in this place. I've heard so many stories about this area from Grandfather."]=1,
},
[201312]={ -- Warpweaver Taxoss
  ["Now is the time when the year is new and the moon shines bright.$B$BIt is our time... when the ancients awake."]=1,
  ["I have all the tools necessary to adjust the appearance of your weapons and armor. Shall we begin?"]=2,
},
[202700]={ -- Lysander Starshade
  ["My sister Nari has always thought of me as a child, despite my years. I am not blind to the problems that have plagued our people--and I will not fail them. I'm here to help, whatever the cost."]=1,
},
[204926]={ -- Delver Mardei
  ["The ecological diversity in these caves is spectacular, adventurer!"]=1,
},
[205067]={ -- Shandris Feathermoon
  ["We must uncover what Fyrakk is plotting."]=1,
},
[205879]={ -- Ethereal Warpweaver
  ["I have all the tools necessary to adjust the appearance of your weapons and armor. Shall we begin?"]=1,
},
[206017]={ -- Brann Bronzebeard
  ["Ah, the adventure of exploring the unknown! There's nothin' like it, eh adventurer?"]=1,
},
[206537]={ -- Rubaen Hillhelm
  ["Where would you like to fly?"]=1,
},
[207350]={ -- Wrathion
  ["We are not alone, adventurer. There are other flights of dragons out there that have yet to make their way to the Isles. Vyranoth has shown in her... unique way that not only can we work with others, we should. Sabellian spoke of a brood in Outland known as the netherwing. I extended an invitation to Valdrakken and their representative has agreed to meet us there."]=1,
  ["I confess, I have not met them myself. However, Sabellian has provided some helpful information. It seems the netherwing originated from black dragon eggs that had been hidden away on Draenor. When the place shattered into Outland, the eggs were infused with the energies of the Twisting Nether. It... changed them into what they are today. They are now entirely separate from Sabellian's brood... but when you think upon it, they are still our direct kin. I suppose we both have bizarre circumstances surrounding our origins."]=2,
},
[207353]={ -- Arko'narin Starshade
  ["Time is of the essence, adventurer."]=1,
},
[208070]={ -- Sir Finley Mrrgglton
  ["Greetings and salutations! What can I do for you?"]=1,
},
[208143]={ -- Keeper Amrymn
  ["Fyrakk's forces are all around us, and we are few in number. Thank you for your efforts in protecting the Dream."]=1,
},
[208156]={ -- Moon Priestess Lasara
  ["Goddess be with you adventurer."]=1,
},
[208669]={ -- Lady Moonberry
  ["This place is just like Ysera described. Beautiful, but strange. It's magnificent!"]=1,
},
[209318]={ -- Cenarius
  ["Welcome to the Dream, champion."]=1,
},
[209330]={ -- Tekazza of the Aimless Few
  ["Where would you like to fly?"]=1,
},
[209790]={ -- Virtos
  ["The Prophet awaits you."]=1,
},
[211209]={ -- Elianna
  ["The magic of the dream is breathtaking!"]=1,
  ["Dream Infusions are powerful coalescences of dream energy that we can use to bring a creature's essence into the Dream."]=2,
  ["I must verify that you can take care of one of these precious creatures before entrusting you with one of their dream kin."]=3,
},
[212370]={ -- Ronesh
  ["Another outlander from the beach, are you? A few of your sector, Anduin and Magni, arrived earlier. They are downstairs. News of your aid to us has traveled through the city. I welcome you and your allies, and will help you as best I can. Although... if you share the same food requirement as your compatriots, your choices are limited. What we consume is unpalatable to you--gems, ore, and cinderbrew. This inn was created because we did have travelers like you once come from below. But, I can see what I have."]=1,
},
[214352]={ -- Rooktender Otwin
  ["The Stormriders are at your service."]=1,
},
[215258]={ -- Clerk Gretal
  ["Welcome adventurer! Would you like to list a crafting order with us today?"]=1,
},
[215520]={ -- Edothir
  ["Welcome, outlander. Your allies arrived earlier. They have been kind in helping my people."]=1,
},
[215563]={ -- Igram Underwing
  ["The sounds of industry ring through the Deeps! Fly to the far-flung reaches of the realm, and you'll hear even greater wonders."]=1,
},
[215800]={ -- Treagor
  ["Treagor's body is crisscrossed with cracks and nerubian poison has almost corroded away his hands and feet. However, fresh and thick mud paste holds him together."]=1,
},
[216094]={ -- Kodun
  ["Welcome to Freywold Village, outlander. We Unbound dedicate our lives to the pursuit of craftsmanship, production, and innovation. The last is what many chase but few find ever."]=1,
},
[216251]={ -- Professor Ash
  ["Hello, adventurer. How can I be of service?"]=1,
},
[216265]={ -- Tel'Athir
  ["I can instruct you in alchemy. Interested?"]=1,
},
[216270]={ -- Ravensmith Ta'lir
  ["I can instruct you in engineering. Interested?"]=1,
},
[216271]={ -- Jelena Nightsky
  ["I can instruct you in skinning. Interested?"]=1,
},
[216284]={ -- Mythrin'dir
  ["Countless lives were lost at Teldrassil. They are gone... But not forgotten."]=1,
},
[216289]={ -- Orokai
  ["Greetings, young druid."]=1,
},
[216450]={ -- Darianna
  ["I can instruct you in leatherworking. Interested?"]=1,
},
[216642]={ -- Archmage Mordent Evenshade
  ["It seems like only mere moments ago I was petitioning for our right to return to kaldorei society. So much has changed since then. The Shen'dralar were no strangers to sorrow. But it warms my heart to see that our kin have achieved a happier end than the highborne of Dire Maul. With so many promising young students of the arcane gathering here, we may need to establish a more permanent place of learning."]=1,
},
[216722]={ -- Captain Talar Oaktalon
  ["Greetings, friend. I am Talar Oaktalon. It has been many years since my first voyage to Gilneas. That was a different time for both of our people. A different world, even. To think now, after all the suffering both kaldorei and Gilneans have endured, we can make this return journey with no trepidation but merely... tranquil purpose. <Talar inhales deeply before exhaling with a smile.> Welcome aboard the Moonlit Rose."]=1,
},
[216803]={ -- Sentinel Eriadnar
  ["Welcome to Belanaar, traveller. May you feel at home for as long as you stay."]=1,
},
[216972]={ -- Courier Lyan
  ["Where would you like to fly?"]=1,
},
[216979]={ -- Roughrider Tany
  ["Where would you like to fly?"]=1,
},
[217080]={ -- Gostrof
  ["Titans preserve you, outlander. If you need supplies taken out of Dornogal or into it, then I'm your quarry! My directive is delivering supplies and trade goods. No matter the recipient."]=1,
},
[217081]={ -- Trader Harthan
  ["Steelvein takes care of those who help him. My crew worked hard to earn his trust."]=1,
},
[217088]={ -- Nernabel
  ["Task... interrupted? I'm a little busy at the moment. If you are here to make an order, please see Uthaga outside!"]=1,
},
[217090]={ -- Loldren
  ["<The earthen doesn't acknowledge you as he pores over the stacks of scrolls and paperwork around him.>"]=1,
},
[217439]={ -- Iridi
  ["Where would you like to fly?"]=1,
},
[217543]={ -- Tordrin
  ["Where would you like to fly?"]=1,
},
[217639]={ -- Auro Flitter
  ["Where would you like to fly?"]=1,
},
[218295]={ -- Bastian Wynfall
  ["Where would you like to fly?"]=1,
},
[218298]={ -- Vellas Tearen
  ["Where would you like to fly?"]=1,
},
[218300]={ -- Gear Flamepierce
  ["Where would you like to fly?"]=1,
},
[218304]={ -- 'Red' Fearon
  ["Where would you like to fly?"]=1,
},
[218305]={ -- Anje Noon
  ["Where would you like to fly?"]=1,
},
[218323]={ -- Tristan Lyte
  ["Where would you like to fly?"]=1,
},
[218388]={ -- Milgrit Stonefeather
  ["Where would you like to fly?"]=1,
},
[219043]={ -- Clerk Ardran
  ["Welcome adventurer! Would you like to list a crafting order with us today?"]=1,
},
[219048]={ -- Clerk Pordaz
  ["Welcome adventurer! Would you like to list a crafting order with us today?"]=1,
},
[219050]={ -- Aisha
  ["That the sands would take you here, $c, welcome. What trade brings you here?"]=1,
},
[219052]={ -- Wireweaver Grelka
  ["It's important to maintain a good wire care routine. But if you've fallen behind, we can help! We offer extending, trimming, recoloring, braiding, coiling, and all other forms of wire management."]=1,
},
[219063]={ -- Ms. Xiulan
  ["We have the most exotic of wares from across the world."]=1,
},
[219080]={ -- Marbb
  ["How may I help you?"]=1,
},
[219083]={ -- Ginnad
  ["How may I help you?"]=1,
},
[219085]={ -- Nagad
  ["How may I help you?"]=1,
},
[219087]={ -- Makir
  ["How may I help you?"]=1,
},
[219090]={ -- Brrigan
  ["How may I help you?"]=1,
},
[219092]={ -- Tarig
  ["How may I help you?"]=1,
},
[219094]={ -- Kotag
  ["How may I help you?"]=1,
},
[219097]={ -- Tarib
  ["How may I help you?"]=1,
},
[219099]={ -- Thermalseer Arhdas
  ["How may I help you?"]=1,
},
[219101]={ -- Akdan
  ["How may I help you?"]=1,
},
[219222]={ -- Lalandi
  ["With every victory, a step forward. With every loss, the same."]=1,
},
[219226]={ -- Vaskarn
  ["Greetings, friend! Even after spending a considerable amount of time in Dornogal, we're still discovering new kinds of crests! These new Ethereal Crests are fascinating little artifacts that combine nicely with Valorstones. And of course, Cuzolth has already developed a way to use them to upgrade your latest adventuring gear. Me? I'm still researching Crest transmutation. As usual. Oh, I'm not complaining. I like being useful to you and the other adventurers. I would... rather stay behind here, myself. I'm not much of a fighter."]=1,
},
[219243]={ -- Teha
  ["Welcome to the grand collaboration between the Zen'shiri Trading Post and the T&W Trading Post!"]=1,
},
[219244]={ -- Andee Seabraid
  ["Welcome to the joint venture of the T&W and Zen'shiri Trading Post!"]=1,
},
[219256]={ -- Badur
  ["Would you like to try an ore treat? I have iron, copper, and gold. What about minerals? I have everything a body needs."]=1,
},
[219376]={ -- Kargand
  ["Greetings, $c. I can help stable your pets or assist you in recovering lost companions."]=1,
  ["Greetings, $c. I can assist you in recovering lost companions."]=2,
},
[219390]={ -- Gortra
  ["Good day, rider. Ready to learn more about how to make your mount truly unique?"]=1,
},
[219431]={ -- Aufta
  ["If you are here for leisure, you will need to book an appointment with the bath matron. But you may need to wait. We are awfully busy right now and in short supply of, well, everything."]=1,
},
[219590]={ -- Magni Bronzebeard
  ["I dunnae need help, adventurer. <Magni winces in pain. He is clearly winded and injured.> Maybe... just a wee leg up on tae a gryphon or whatever these birds be..."]=1,
},
[219591]={ -- Moira Thaurissan
  ["O' course we get stranded here an' the first thing me da' goes an' does is get himself injured. Always got tae play the hero. I hope Dagran does nae get any ideas. But who am I kiddin'? Whisked away tae a far off place an' stranded? Meetin' a tall, dark dwarf when I get there? I can talk me way out o' this. Bring it on, Khaz Algar."]=1,
},
[219592]={ -- Dagran Thaurissan II
  ["I've got all me books an' scrolls but... Look at all we've lost. All the knowledge stored in Dalaran. All o' the people... I hope these earthen find more survivors. An' I hope that granda' bein' a 'thraegar' can help us be friends with them. Maybe they'll have a library too. Wouldn't that be grand?"]=1,
},
[219594]={ -- Anduin Wrynn
  ["Death... and destruction. Everywhere. At every turn, I lose more friends. More family. Khadgar. Alleria... Will it end with Xal'atath? When will it end?"]=1,
},
[219595]={ -- Thrall
  ["Xal'atath must be stopped. Let us hope that these earthen do not hinder us."]=1,
},
[219596]={ -- Lady Jaina Proudmoore
  ["I am glad that the earthen found us when they did. But I fear that we may need more than their help if we wish to mount an offensive against the nerubians and Xal'atath."]=1,
},
[221002]={ -- Khole
  ["Welcome to the latest expansion to the Trading Post! Almost every month new and exotic creatures will arrive. You can see some of the latest creatures we have to trade right here."]=1,
},
[221074]={ -- Assistant Darragh Irongut
  ["Every month we get new outfits and weapons from all over. It's my job to make sure these outfits and weapons are properly displayed."]=1,
},
[221077]={ -- Assistant Ula Threadstrong
  ["New shipments of outfits, weapons and creatures come in every month. I make sure our displays always look their best."]=1,
},
[221390]={ -- Waxmonger Squick
  ["This not junk. This treasure!"]=1,
},
[221848]={ -- Warpweaver Voxin
  ["Now is the time when the year is new and the moon shines bright.$B$BIt is our time... when the ancients awake."]=1,
  ["I have all the tools necessary to adjust the appearance of your weapons and armor. Shall we begin?"]=2,
},
[222218]={ -- Peacekeeper Lieutenant
  ["The Peacekeepers protect Dornogal from all threats, foreign and domestic. We also provide assistance and render aid to our fellow citizens and foreign travelers. We are not charged with the defense of the isle as a whole. That responsibility falls to the Stormriders. Peacekeepers must stay and serve within the limits of Dornogal. Over the years, some peacekeepers, like Aggartha and Leif, have the ridiculous notion that we must venture forth beyond the city to fulfill our purpose. A noble, but misguided sentiment. We know our duty and we will fulfill it exactly as we have been ordered."]=1,
},
[222259]={ -- Concerned Dornogal Citizen
  ["After thousands of years, I know almost every face in Dornogal. But I do not know yours. Have a seat, friend!"]=1,
},
[222260]={ -- Concerned Dornogal Citizen
  ["Ugh, more strangers. Why are you talking to me?"]=1,
},
[222263]={ -- Concerned Dornogal Citizen
  ["More and more newcomers enter the city every day. Their interference has disrupted a routine I have kept for a thousand years. <The earthen sighs.> What is it I can do for you?"]=1,
},
[222315]={ -- Lamplighter Kaerter
  ["You'd think it'd be easier to get information from these earthen. It's like talking to a bunch of rocks! ...what?"]=1,
},
[222334]={ -- Freywold Constable
  ["Our people started going missing when the Arathi first arrived. At first we thought our neighbors had simply gone out of town but more and more started disappearing. We questioned the Arathi but they denied any wrongdoing. Then, one morning, we discovered the Arathi had left in the night. We have been combing the countryside searching for them and our people, to no avail."]=1,
},
[222631]={ -- Archmage Celindra
  ["I do not believe you possess the mental acuity to grasp the nature of portal magic."]=1,
  ["As a mage, you are one of a select group that can conjure a portal to transport you back to this very place. I can teach you if you are ready."]=2,
},
[223254]={ -- Queen Ansurek
  ["<The shadecaster projects an image of Queen Ansurek, spreading her lies to all who stop to listen.>"]=1,
},
[223440]={ -- Silvia
  ["We will fight for Lady Shandris, whenever she calls."]=1,
},
[223460]={ -- Mariner Everwatch
  ["Many have been lost to the seas. I, and the wisps, are charged with looking for those souls."]=1,
},
[223462]={ -- Mariner Softsong
  ["We must make sure not to lose any more souls to the seas."]=1,
},
[223470]={ -- Mariner Moonblade
  ["We must make sure not to lose any more souls to the seas."]=1,
},
[223471]={ -- Mariner Stillwake
  ["Forgive me $c, but I must concentrate on my job."]=1,
},
[223484]={ -- Captain Idrilae
  ["When old Oaktalon asked me to join his crew on the Moonlit Rose, I...well, I almost considered it. Captaining the Feathermoon Ferry had given me so much through all my years. But after seeing the splendor of Amirdrassil, I realized I had forgotten to appreciate the new wonders of world. My crew, however, was keen for new waters to sail. They'll serve the Rose faithfully. For me? It is time to enjoy and embrace my retirement. I think I will explore these isles before I settle in and call them home."]=1,
},
[223533]={ -- Custodian Khubon
  ["Ah, the Catalyst. It's a marvel that even words struggle to capture. Picture this, if you can: long before our city's foundations were laid, the titan's famed keepers roamed this earth. Masters of innovation, they forged wonders beyond our imagination. And amidst their great works, they crafted this Catalyst."]=1,
},
[223648]={ -- Betta
  ["Hello, outlander. What brings you to my home?"]=1,
},
[223649]={ -- Maluc
  ["Hello, outlander. Welcome to Freywold."]=1,
},
[223652]={ -- Kurron
  ["So many outsiders all of a sudden, bringing many outlandish ideas. A great change is upon us."]=1,
},
[223923]={ -- Natalia Pearce
  ["What took you so long? Those raging elementals could have killed me! I mean, luckily they didn't see me, but you could have gotten here a bit faster! <Natalia lets out an annoyed sigh.> Let me know when you are ready to enter the cave."]=1,
},
[224708]={ -- Cenderragg
  ["Since you're here, perhaps you can help out?"]=1,
},
[224884]={ -- Clixi Fastfare
  ["Lookin' for a lift? Best deal right here, pal. actually, it's the only deal! I'm the boss of this sky market, see? So, where's it you're headed today?"]=1,
},
[224940]={ -- Kargen Ironbrow
  ["Where would you like to fly?"]=1,
},
[225347]={ -- Stormrider Bruelda
  ["The Stormriders shall always endure."]=1,
},
[226250]={ -- Reno Jackson
  ["If you need it, we found it."]=1,
},
[226287]={ -- Ellerdin
  ["Mountains tremble before you, outlander. I am an expert at people watching. You, for example, look like you love rocking super sweet gear."]=1,
},
[226838]={ -- Opalcreg Worker
  ["This could be our last chance, we can't give up yet."]=1,
},
[227118]={ -- Meredy Huntswell
  ["Hello, adventurer! If you need some help in the Rookery, let me know. The other followers are ready to help. So am I."]=1,
},
[227675]={ -- Delver's Guide
  ["<This book contains all the information documented on delves and delve-related things.>"]=1,
},
[227758]={ -- Alleria Windrunner
  ["What news do you bring, adventurer?"]=1,
},
[227853]={ -- Pix Xizzix
  ["Impulse purchases are the most fun kind of purchases!"]=1,
},
[228137]={ -- Jix
  ["Where would you like to fly?"]=1,
},
[228605]={ -- Elise Starseeker
  ["I appreciate your help with the cipher key, but you'll have to excuse me for a moment. This map won't read itself."]=1,
},
[229029]={ -- Gilbertha
  ["It's my duty to check in on every cat in Dornogal, but I can't find Ruufus! I am beyond thrilled that Sheaf is exactly where he was yesterday."]=1,
},
[229075]={ -- Scalecommander Emberthal
  ["I'm glad we were able to get you out, adventurer. We haven't been so lucky in some of the other creches we've uncovered."]=1,
},
[230235]={ -- Skaggit
  ["Heya, pal! Ready to embark on a thrilling adventure?"]=1,
},
[230246]={ -- Li Li Stormstout
  ["Oh, hey there! I've been waiting for someone to come along! Lorewalker Cho told me to sit here and tell stories to anyone who would listen, as a part of my apprenticeship to be a Lorewalker. I thought maybe he was pranking me, but here you are! Would you like to hear a story?"]=1,
},
[230317]={ -- Mokvar
  ["Thrall has shown great kindness in granting me sanctuary within his domain. I do not wish to overstay my welcome, at any rate. It would be a great dishonor if I brought any trouble to our leader."]=1,
},
[230736]={ -- Om'talad
  ["Locus-Walker sent word ahead that you might be showing up here. Between his word and yours, I will trust that the Wastelanders are not here for plunder."]=1,
},
[231039]={ -- Arator
  ["Champion, thank you for coming. Your skills are renown throughout Azeroth and beyond. I hope you can help us."]=1,
},
[231042]={ -- Vereesa Windrunner
  ["Thank you for coming. The Radiant Song has been singing to me. It's... her visions come and go, but they're vague. Destruction, screaming, death. Since we came here, the visions have become stronger and more painful. I can manage. We have much to discuss and not much time, I fear."]=1,
},
[231534]={ -- Captain Krazz
  ["Man, am I glad to be back in the air again! Well, I guess 'consulting' is more the correct term. For a sea voyage as long this, it only makes sense they pulled a seasoned pilot like myself out of retirement! I did even fly a Warchief or two into battle after all. I hear this island has a lotta storms or somethin'. Ah, it reminds me of my days back in the Second War, ferry'n troops around... <Captain Kazz grins widely.> Anyway, Cableclamp is a great captain, so rest assured she'll getcha where ya need to go."]=1,
},
[231538]={ -- Fergus Gearchum
  ["It's good to be serve'n under Captain Krazz again, though I will say I'm equally excited to be able to work with Sky-Captain Cableclamp! Her laid back attitude is legendary. I'm glad she was able to find work after the Purple Princess's zeppelin circuit from Brill to Grom'gol was, uh, 'decommissioned'."]=1,
},
[231540]={ -- Scalecommander Azurathel
  ["Welcome back, $c. The Obsidian Warders are working through our creches, finding our lost kin. The world you are stepping into is very different than when we slept. The Obsidian Warders are part of the Alliance now, one of the two major factions of Azeroth. I'll let you form your own opinions, but I think you'll like them."]=1,
},
[231541]={ -- Sky-Captain Cableclamp
  ["Sure feels good to be back flyin' on the open breeze after a few years! Say, you thinkin' about headin' back to Dornogal?"]=1,
  ["Welcome aboard, $c! The Princess's Pride is nearly ready to head back to the Siren Isle! You ready to go?"]=2,
},
[231544]={ -- Scalecommander Cindrethresh
  ["Welcome back, $c. The Dark Talons are working through our creches, finding our lost kin. The world you are stepping into is very different than when we slept. The Dark Talons are part of the Horde now, one of the two major factions of Azeroth. I'll let you form your own opinions, but I think you'll like them."]=1,
},
[231820]={ -- Ve'nari
  ["Ah, you are here. Good. There is work to be done."]=1,
},
[231919]={ -- Botanist Alaenra
  ["So, why did you portal here?"]=1,
},
[232648]={ -- Slateback Alpha
  ["<The slateback alpha eyes you as you approach.>"]=1,
},
[233019]={ -- Renzik "The Shiv"
  ["I've got your six covered. Go steal some bombs so we can blast our way into that dam!"]=1,
},
[233252]={ -- Vereesa Windrunner
  ["Thank you for doing this, adventurer. I miss my husband so much."]=1,
},
[233253]={ -- Arator
  ["I'm worried about my aunt, adventurer. These visions are getting worse and I'm afraid of what they'll do to her."]=1,
},
[233312]={ -- Arator
  ["That must have been Silvermoon in Vereesa's vision. I hope it's wrong. But if not, we must prepare the city's defenses."]=1,
},
[233346]={ -- Thorntail Matriarch
  ["<The thorntail matriarch watches you as you approach.>"]=1,
},
[233603]={ -- Locus-Walker
  ["I'm glad you are here. I will need your help, as well as Alleria's."]=1,
},
[235252]={ -- Om'sirik
  ["Welcome stranger, to Om'sirik's wonder emporium!"]=1,
},
[235612]={ -- Scramblington Spoonfork
  ["Well well well... you want in on my operation? Sorry little buddy, no one's ever satisfied with just one piece. Get your money up and maybe you can do business with a guy like me."]=1,
},
[235615]={ -- Lathe Faceter
  ["Still ironing out the bugs - all this revolution has me feeling a little overstimulated. Wanna try out Faceter's Face-Lifter? It won't make you good as new - it'll make you even better!"]=1,
},
[235617]={ -- Paula Piranha
  ["Hey sweetie! We're so happy to welcome you enjoy the thrills of playing at the Gallagio! ... or that's what I would say, if there wasn't a revolution goin' on. The Boss is paranoid, hidin' somewhere inside and kicked a lot of us out to make room for his hired muscle. I'm not sure what all the fuss is about, but I'm more than happy to see to your every need. Even if you end up wrecking the place, the Gallagio treasures your loyalty. Win big & spend bigger, baby!"]=1,
},
[235620]={ -- Sando the Rat
  ["Boss says I'm not 'spose to tell strangers we got counterfeit weapons, on account of they ain't real, so's it's easier to sell 'em to tourists thinkin' they IS real. So don't tell anyone. *Specially* not a stranger."]=1,
},
[235621]={ -- Ando the Gat
  ["Yeah, we're affiliated with the Gallagio. Who's askin? ...You are? To me? Right now? Well, my associate and I don't talk to small timers, and neither does our inventory. Beat it. |cFFFF0000[Requires Renown 17 with the Gallagio Loyalty Rewards Club.]|r"]=1,
},
[235626]={ -- Lynndy Leatherbolts
  ["Welcome adventurer! Would you like to list a crafting order with us today?"]=1,
},
[235787]={ -- Lor'themar Theron
  ["Silvermoon is grateful for your aid."]=1,
},
[235895]={ -- Seeker Najed
  ["Have you lost something important? I can return it. For a price."]=1,
},
[236057]={ -- Watcher Umjin
  ["Feels good to be back on de open air! Never felt right after we all went on strike with Cableclamp. Her contractors weren't payin' any of us--her included! So she brought the Princess down. Eventually we went our own separate ways for a while. But we be back and ready to fly! Ha ha! Except Du'una. She's afraid of de bwon'tulak, which I don't blame her. We're sailin' right into stormy weathers, but Shango always watchin' over us in de storms!"]=1,
},
[236058]={ -- Watcher Du'una
  ["You headin' to the Siren Isle? <Du'una grimaces around her tusks and spits.> I told Cableclamp dis is a bad omen. I've heard stories about de sirens. In zandali, we call dem 'bwon'tulak.' Death Singers. Terrible creatures. I am blessed. I never encountered dem before in all my time flyin' over de seas. But now we're headin' for a place named after dem? <Du'una bows and shakes her head.> May Shango guide de winds."]=1,
},
[236704]={ -- Orweyna
  ["We must not delay. It is time for me to return to Harandar."]=1,
},
[237209]={ -- Ku'paal
  ["It is forbidden to bring outsiders to Harandar! Orweyna broke our laws by going to the surface and letting your world know about us. And now this? You are lucky that Orweyna is a friend. Otherwise I would bind you in roots and leave you to the saptors."]=1,
},
[237210]={ -- Orweyna
  ["Harandar lies below and beyond. The swirl of roots above is the Cradle, a most holy place related to the goddess, Aln'hara. Below is Har'athir, the paint maker's village. Let's stop here for a moment. My eyes and heart desire to look upon my homeland, after so long away."]=1,
  ["Let us move on to Har'athir. I do not expect we will have a warm welcome. Check on Halduron and see if he's ready to move on."]=2,
},
[237341]={ -- Halduron Brightwing
  ["This is astonishing. An entire world at the end of the rootways. How Harandar managed to stay hidden all these countless centuries is an incredible feat. The Lightbloom is our focus, but I admit I am intrigued to learn more about the haranir and their world within our world."]=1,
},
[237343]={ -- Halduron Brightwing
  ["To think that we are beneath the roots of the great World Trees. It is breathtaking. We never knew there was an entire world here. This is a precious opportunity that no one else in Azeroth has been granted. I am ready to move on when you are."]=1,
},
[237480]={ -- Orweyna
  ["It feels good to be home and to touch the roots of Harandar. I have been too long away."]=1,
},
[237504]={ -- Grand Magister Rommath
  ["No agent of the void will escape our watch. I hold everyone in suspicion."]=1,
},
[237506]={ -- Magister Umbric
  ["The Twilight's Blade are a collection of fools. Fools who have been conscripted by Xal'atath."]=1,
},
[237865]={ -- Danul
  ["Where did you come from? I've never seen anything like you before, in all my years!"]=1,
},
[237866]={ -- Oorla
  ["How did you get here, trespasser? It is forbidden for outsiders to come to Harandar!"]=1,
},
[237995]={ -- Darla Fluxy
  ["I'm an expert in all things professions. You need me to blow your mind?"]=1,
},
[238148]={ -- Norb
  ["Yeah, Dornogal's definitely gotta pay for this. Our drill operator had to swerve to avoid that giant underground tunnel thing. Bent half the blades outta shape and made him spill his latte. The latte's the more expensive claim, actually."]=1,
},
[238149]={ -- Oathsworn Administrator
  ["The Councilward rejects their request for payment. If this goblin would like to argue the matter, so be it. He requires sleep cycles eventually. I do not."]=1,
},
[238209]={ -- Cartel Om Custodian
  ["What? I'm very busy. If you want to talk, it can wait until you have completed your first task. <You can hear muttering as they turn away.> Honestly, it's so hard to find good help."]=1,
},
[238239]={ -- Cartel Om Custodian
  ["I am so very sorry. I had no idea you were... well... you! Please accept my apologies. I would not have asked you to perform this task if I had known."]=1,
},
[238902]={ -- Sky Hunter Perennius
  ["The skies darken with the Legion's forces. Let us take the fight to them."]=1,
},
[239665]={ -- Hatheon
  ["Welcome to the Bank of Silvermoon, sir. Would you care to access the depository?"]=1,
  ["Thank you for choosing the Bank of Silvermoon. What may I do for you today?"]=2,
},
[239670]={ -- Vaultkeeper Elysa
  ["How may I help you?"]=1,
},
[240523]={ -- Scouting Map
  ["Where should we focus our efforts?"]=1,
},
[240715]={ -- Halduron Brightwing
  ["This is an unparalleled opportunity to see the homeland of the haranir. They have been so secretive that not even a whisper of Harandar has come to us through the roots of the World Trees."]=1,
},
[241141]={ -- Erus
  ["Erus scrap junk for you."]=1,
},
[241142]={ -- Momentus
  ["There are few problems that a little heat and a hammer cannot solve."]=1,
},
[241143]={ -- Durus
  ["Keep your shield up, and patience will see you through any battle."]=1,
},
[241145]={ -- Aeonicus
  ["Oh, a time walker! I bet you've got stories to tell."]=1,
},
[241147]={ -- Arturos
  ["Good to see you, champion! How fare your hunts?"]=1,
},
[241167]={ -- Horos
  ["We will have everything in time."]=1,
},
[241168]={ -- Pythagorus
  ["What do you need, puny $r?"]=1,
},
[241179]={ -- Nostwin
  ["<Nostwin munches on something delicious.>"]=1,
},
[241182]={ -- Hemet Nesingwary XVII
  ["The name's Hemet Nesingwary, tha seventeenth. Surely you've 'eard of my esteemed and grand familial lineage."]=1,
},
[241184]={ -- Agos the Silent
  ["<Agos gives you a knowing nod.>"]=1,
},
[241185]={ -- Infinite Armoredon
  ["<The Infinite Armoredon regards you with mild interest.>"]=1,
},
[241186]={ -- Grandmaster Jakkus
  ["Ah, welcome young $c! I remember my $c training like it was yesterday."]=1,
},
[241191]={ -- Larah Treebender
  ["Oh honey, you need a new look."]=1,
},
[241193]={ -- Hooded Supplier
  ["I have no business with you, $c."]=1,
},
[241507]={ -- Om'volt
  ["Avail yourself of the Oasis's amenities."]=1,
},
[241677]={ -- Image of Lady Liadrin
  ["Xal'atath and her Devouring Host have attacked the Sunwell on the Isle of Quel'Danas. The Light has called to you for help, adventurer."]=1,
},
[241703]={ -- Silvermoon Guard
  ["What do you seek, priest?"]=1,
},
[241748]={ -- Eternus
  ["Time is as varied as it is infinite."]=1,
  ["You have learned much and taught us more. The sands are slipping away quickly now and this timeline will soon be closed to us. Learn what else you can in the time we have left to us, then we must go and seek a safer timeline."]=2,
},
[241882]={ -- Brewfest Reveler
  ["I am ready to order."]=1,
  ["Bring me a drink!"]=2,
  ["I would like some soup."]=3,
},
[242492]={ -- Kristoff Snowbellow
  ["Welcome to the Holiday Hub!"]=1,
},
[242723]={ -- Apprentice Diell
  ["How may I help you?"]=1,
},
[242724]={ -- Ranger Allorn
  ["How may I help you?"]=1,
},
[242725]={ -- Armorer Goldcrest
  ["How may I help you?"]=1,
},
[242726]={ -- Neriv
  ["How may I help you?"]=1,
},
[243198]={ -- Ingredient Wagon
  ["Choose your ingredients."]=1,
},
[243229]={ -- Eldara Dawnrunner
  ["A sight to behold, is it not? Since the time of Dath'Remar, the elves have used this great forge to craft armor of unparalleled might. It is said that the flames were first stoked by the soul of a phoenix who thought it a fitting nest, and that its power still weaves itself through every creation. We will permit you to share in its gifts."]=1,
  ["The Catalyst can infuse great power into items, enhancing them and pushing their potential further than ever before!"]=2,
},
[243280]={ -- Theremis
  ["Which Midnight Specialization would you like to relearn?"]=1,
},
[243349]={ -- Dolothos
  ["Greetings. Are you seeking instruction in enchanting?"]=1,
},
[243357]={ -- Camberon
  ["Greetings. Are you seeking instruction in alchemy?"]=1,
},
[243853]={ -- Moratari
  ["Don't forget to record your data points."]=1,
},
[244485]={ -- Distributor Ba'nacl
  ["I can instruct you in fishing, and sell fishing poles and supplies.$B$BHow may I help you?"]=1,
},
[244544]={ -- Brewfest Reveler
  ["I am ready to order."]=1,
  ["Bring me a drink!"]=2,
  ["I would like some soup."]=3,
  ["I'm craving a pretzel."]=4,
},
[244545]={ -- Brewfest Reveler
  ["I am ready to order."]=1,
  ["I'm craving a pretzel."]=2,
  ["I would like some soup."]=3,
},
[244705]={ -- Brewfest Reveler
  ["I'm craving a pretzel."]=1,
  ["I am ready to order."]=2,
},
[244749]={ -- Xy'dax
  ["Danger's part of the deal, but so is unprecedented profit."]=1,
},
[244792]={ -- Lindormi
  ["Tales of adventure are the best! Dark dungeons, terrifying monsters, shiny treasures... I want to hear all about them! If you promise to bring back a good story, I might even let you borrow a keystone."]=1,
},
[244808]={ -- Aramis Hammerhand
  ["Welcome back to the light, friend. Do you require training?"]=1,
  ["You may not be a paladin, but you may yet find solace in the light should you seek it."]=2,
},
[245102]={ -- Dalnir
  ["Tending the roots takes time and dedication, which are the two building blocks of a healthy tradition."]=1,
},
[245282]={ -- Warpweaver Lo'rant
  ["Now is the time when the year is new and the moon shines bright.$B$BIt is our time... when the ancients awake."]=1,
  ["I have all the tools necessary to adjust the appearance of your weapons and armor. Shall we begin?"]=2,
},
[246026]={ -- Unicus
  ["Styles change all the time, but nothing stays out of style forever."]=1,
},
[246028]={ -- Sacerdormu
  ["Why choose between substance and style when you can have both? Just not from me, not anymore. Pythagorus has what you're looking for now."]=1,
},
[246030]={ -- Freddie Threads
  ["Hey there, kitty-cat, you look like you could use some threads."]=1,
},
[246152]={ -- Shari Stilwell
  ["The light is a beacon that shines for all. What can I do for you, paladin?"]=1,
},
[246154]={ -- Suspicious Citizen
  ["This world doesn't deserve you, $c. How often do you run to its rescue? We value you. We know what you could be with the right help."]=1,
  ["Has the Light left you in the dark? You're not alone in these shadows. She's here to show us a better way."]=2,
  ["The end is coming. It's always approaching. What will you do when it finally arrives?"]=3,
  ["There's always another struggle on Azeroth. What if you could leave it all behind? What if you could become something more?"]=4,
  ["You seek peace. Quiet. Rest. I know where you can find all that and more."]=5,
},
[246155]={ -- Suspicious Citizen
  ["Have you tasted darkness, $c? May I offer you some? <They reach a hand into their pocket.>"]=1,
  ["<They look left and right before leaning in too close.> Know anything about the Radiant Song? It just never ends."]=2,
  ["Hello. I'm conducting market research. On a scale of one to ten, how likely are you to surrender to that unsettling voice in your head?"]=3,
  ["Are you interested in a gathering of select, elite individuals dedicated to studying matters most would shy away from? We meet on the second moonrise of every third month."]=4,
},
[246349]={ -- Breton Samuels
  ["Welcome to Bandarion Keep, mage."]=1,
},
[246378]={ -- Danitha Morr
  ["Welcome to Bandarion Keep, mage."]=1,
},
[246389]={ -- Hilda the Breaker
  ["Why do they call me 'The Breaker'? Trust me, you don't want to know."]=1,
},
[246393]={ -- Jorin Croge
  ["There are many things lurking out there in the dark and the light is needed now more than ever. If only these poor souls could see that just because our world has changed, that doesn't mean we have to be the monsters that the living think we are."]=1,
},
[246394]={ -- Ander Solliden
  ["In my previous life, I lived nearby here. I still wander the fields of my childhood farmstead occasionally. It fills me with sadness to see those I knew and loved, shambling around as mindless thralls. It pains me, but its that very pain that gives me strength and purpose."]=1,
  ["In my previous life, I lived nearby here. I still wander the fields of my childhood farmstead occasionally. It fills me with sadness to see those I knew and loved, shambling around as mindless thralls. It pains me, but it's that very pain that gives me strength and purpose."]=1,
},
[246607]={ -- Greenspeaker Cyenna
  ["We are blessed to live in Harandar, and we treat that as a responsibility. The roots of World Trees wind through these lands, and we must tend to them to make sure that they continue to thrive. I am Cyenna, Charge Nurse of Nordrassil. It is a responsibility I take very seriously."]=1,
},
[246848]={ -- Kirin Tor Guard
  ["What are you looking for?"]=1,
  ["What is your curiosity looking for?"]=2,
},
[248196]={ -- Apothecary Durelle
  ["Please do not touch the vials unless you intend to purchase one. Fingerprints ruin the value, you see."]=1,
},
[248197]={ -- Gor'mak
  ["You won't find better equipment anywhere else!"]=1,
},
[248200]={ -- Fizzlefuse
  ["Yo, what do you need?"]=1,
},
[248201]={ -- Pawani
  ["Greetings, friend! I have ample supply of leather and hides, and I know a few techniques I might be willing to share. Interested in doing business?"]=1,
  ["Greetings, friend! I have an ample supply of leather and hides, and I know a few techniques I might be willing to share. Interested in doing business?"]=2,
},
[248202]={ -- Jim'bek
  ["Jim'bek locks eyes with you as he takes a deep puff from his hookah. 'Ello, mon. Need a rug? A blanket? Or just some cloth for your next project? I got you."]=1,
},
[248351]={ -- Zip Stickshift
  ["Did you know that with a beefy enough hydraulic press and a little help from our patent pending stabilization process, you can compress all this worldsoul nonsense into a nice, compact, and, most importantly, marketable crystal that's got a fragment of somethin' important in it? Mostly just quotes from big wigs, it turns out, but who doesn't want to have the Lich King on something that could reasonably be considered adjacent to speed dial? They also only work in delves for some reason, which is why we set up shop here."]=1,
},
[248415]={ -- Tordrin Sternblade
  ["I kinnae help ye with trainin'. Ye should look fer a warlock trainer."]=1,
},
[248948]={ -- Tome of History
  ["<A heavy tome floats before you. What do you wish to learn?>"]=1,
},
[249041]={ -- Sandee Seabraid
  ["Welcome to the joint venture of the T&W and Zen'shiri Trading Post!"]=1,
},
[249046]={ -- Assistant Shadala
  ["New shipments of outfits, weapons and creatures come in every month. I make sure our displays always look their best."]=1,
},
[249187]={ -- Envoy Manat
  ["It is a great honor to represent Harandar in this grand city."]=1,
  ["Our banner should be outside by the natural beauty of the goddess, not locked within a hut."]=2,
},
[249317]={ -- Pageturner Metros
  ["Need something? I've got theories to sort through."]=1,
},
[249363]={ -- Yala Windwatcher
  ["The Wind Spirits have left us. Now, only mindless echoes remain. Be wary, however. These winds are neither kind, nor gentle."]=1,
  ["The Wind Spirits have left us. Now, only mindless echoes now remain. Be wary, however. These winds are neither kind, nor gentle."]=1,
},
[249468]={ -- Seridis
  ["Do you require something? I am quite busy tending to my lord's hawkstrider."]=1,
},
[249499]={ -- Talenia Flamesong
  ["Hey there, sparkle. Care to make a request? I have a space open in the queue."]=1,
},
[249592]={ -- Titan Console
  ["Static crackling Hello, is this on? It's Dagran. Dagran Thaurissan the second. Do you remember me? Adventurer, I had to return to the Archive, but I updated this console to allow me to communicate with you from there in case you returned. I can also modify the Titan tech remotely via the console so we should be set. Interact with the console if you need to contact me about your Titan tech! A low crackling fades."]=1,
},
[249713]={ -- Odd Child
  ["Shhh! You'll give away my hiding spot!"]=1,
},
[250189]={ -- Irritated Noble
  ["These weak minded fools are beginning to bore me, but I will persist as is socially expected. Where did that waiter go? I need a drink for this."]=1,
},
[250190]={ -- Irritated Noble
  ["These weak minded fools are beginning to bore me, but I will persist as is socially expected. Where did that waiter go? I need a drink for this."]=1,
},
[250686]={ -- Tabitha Heartweaver
  ["Praise to the Banshee Queen, it isn't often I have visitors out here."]=1,
},
[250929]={ -- Malfunctioning Cyclone Construct
  ["<As you approach the enormous cyclone construct, you hear a faint buzzing emanating from beneath its massive armor plates. If you listen carefully you think you might be able to hear a few words being formed but they are too distorted to make out.>"]=1,
},
[251001]={ -- Deathguard Kristof
  ["What are you looking for?"]=1,
  ["Please do see that he reads it at once. I fear our Scourge problem has only just begun. Come see me again in due time. I believe I have nearly uncovered something I could use a willing blade to help with."]=2,
},
[251042]={ -- Domelius
  ["A warm welcome, time walker. Feel free to browse some of my unique home improvement options. Each thematically appropriate for this time and place."]=1,
},
[251361]={ -- Rorian the Dayseeker
  ["What do you need of me, child of Zephras?"]=1,
},
[251362]={ -- Ailee Farheart
  ["Hello, druid."]=1,
  ["Hello, $c."]=1,
},
[251371]={ -- Falorne Fallwind
  ["Greetings to you, fellow High Order initiate."]=1,
  ["Zephras is in great danger. The elemental wind spirits that brought us here to Skywall so many thousands of years ago have abandoned us, leaving us vulnerable in this unstable realm. Our once-robust society spanned multiple island sanctuaries in our corner of Skywall, but now we are not even sure if any other shen'dorei remain outside of this small island. Things are dire, but the High Order is committed to rising to this challenge."]=2,
  ["Magic can accomplish almost anything, but stagnation and inaction have caused us to lose so much of ourselves in the thousands of years since we left Kalimdor. The High Order seeks to reclaim the Highborne heritage that we've left behind and become the masters of our own destiny once again. The Windshapers think we are simply reckless and arrogant. Hypocrisy at its finest, if you ask me. The Windshapers will entertain no ideas but their own when it comes to this crisis. Who, I wonder, is truly arrogant?"]=3,
},
[251373]={ -- Xyton Silverwind
  ["If you have the aptitude for the druidic arts, I can train you."]=1,
},
[251374]={ -- Windshaper Boro
  ["The spirits of the wind may have left us, but the power of the elements is not entirely out of reach for those with the patience to seek them out. If you are initiated in the ways of the shaman, I can help you grasp them."]=1,
},
[251389]={ -- Akeri Duskblade
  ["Slay your enemies and swoon your paramours with this one weird trick. If you follow the path of the rogue, I can teach you... for a cost, of course."]=1,
},
[251487]={ -- Ventaari Brightwish
  ["What may I do for you, fellow windshaper?"]=1,
  ["Zephras is in a state of decline, unfortunately. The elemental wind spirits that brought us here to Skywall so many thousands of years ago have vanished, causing us to lose much of the magic on which we've depended for millennia. The island itself is also dangerously unstable, and we've even lost contact with the other island provinces of the shen'dorei. The few Windshapers that still possess the gift of skysight have attempted to contact our brothers and sisters on the other islands, but we have had no response. Many among us are worried that the shen'dorei here on Zephras are all that is left of our people."]=2,
  ["The shen'dorei will always owe the spirits a debt for their aid, and the Windshapers have sworn an oath to repay that debt and restore things to the way they were before. Unfortunately, we are dangerously blind to what is happening around us within Skywall without the spirits to guide us. The High Order are shortsighted and arrogant, just like their Highborne ancestors. They seek to master and control the magic of this place. This is very path that led us to flee from Kalimdor and reside here in the first place. I fear that much like our forebears their confidence has vastly outpaced their competence and the end result could be disastrous."]=3,
},
[251523]={ -- Constable Aonda
  ["<Constable Aonda wears an intense look on her face, clearly deep in thought.>"]=1,
},
[251662]={ -- Living Lightning
  ["The roiling cloud of living lightning before you seems to crackle menacingly as you approach. It might be best to leave. Quickly."]=1,
},
[251684]={ -- Strange Hermit
  ["H-Hello. You'll have to excuse me, I'm used to your kind running from me."]=1,
  ["That is... a very good question. I have a hard time remembering things, but I do remember something... 'Engineer', perhaps? I think that's what, or who, I was. Other than that all I can seem to remember is soaring through the sky, then seeing a flash of lightning before things got very bumpy. Then... a crash. It's been... a long time though. A very long time."]=2,
  ["Oh these things? I built them. My little friends helped me. I'm not very good at remembering things, but, um, I do know that at one point I used to build a lot of things. Big things! But then, like I said... I was here. The things I build aren't so big and impressive anymore. Still makes me h-happy, heh. B-but... If you want, I can show you how to build things too!"]=3,
  ["Oh, that's okay. I-I'll be here if you want to learn some other time. T-Thank you for talking to me!"]=4,
},
[251902]={ -- Illaya Amberwind
  ["Greetings, child. I am Illaya Amberwind and I am the Elder Windshaper here on Zephras Isle. It's always nice to meet young new faces that make their way down from the grove. Don't let this old shaman hold you up, no doubt you've got many adventures to see to. Do feel free to stop by later if you'd like."]=1,
  ["Where to begin? Our home is failing. The wards have fallen and the three provinces have begun to drift apart. There was a time not long ago when the spires of Shen'dramar were visible from the western watchtower. No longer. The anchor pylons are weakening, and if the chains finally break..."]=2,
  ["Why is this happening? Put simply, the spirits of the wind just... vanished. They were there one day, and they were gone the next. I can't quite describe the feeling that we windshapers felt when it happened. It was as if a great silence fell over all of us and then... a profound absence. The petty wraiths you've likely encountered out there are just shades of the glory of the true spirits of wind. Non-sentient, aimless, and a far cry from the kindly spirits we lived in harmony alongside for thousands of years."]=3,
  ["Many disagree on this point. I believe that simple communication is the key. The songs of the wind rang so clearly to us when the spirits where still here. Since they left, its grown quiet and our power as windshapers has weakened. However, there are those of us who can still hear something. A hushed tone. Fragments of a melody. Those that can still hear and see into the elemental planes must grow in strength. I believe that is the key to our salvation."]=4,
  ["The Cult? They are zealots and killers. They believe that we are being punished for some unspecific sin. The reality is that those that lead them are opportunists leftover from a dubious order of so-called 'Priests' of Al'Akir, the Windlord. They now find themselves in a position to weaponize the fear of our people to consolidate their own power... and they have been quick to do so."]=5,
  ["In all of our years dealing with the wind spirits, at no point did they speak of the Windlord as a figure of reverence. They acknowledged the existence of a being named Al'Akir, but they avoided invoking his name, almost as if they feared him. Even if this Al'Akir is an all-powerful 'Windlord' or ruler of the wind elementals, my centuries of communion with the spirits has convinced me that at the very least he is not universally loved amongst the denizens of Skywall. I fear that attempting to treat with Al'Akir could merely hasten our doom."]=6,
  ["You must remember that while this realm has been our home for millennia, we will always be somewhat alien to this place. We are not in the terrestrial world that birthed our people. We are in the realm of Skywall, a part of the elemental plane. We arrived here as the guests of spirits with whom we found common cause in ages past. Now that we Shen'dorei find ourselves bereft of their presence--and potentially--their protection, there's no telling how the other denizens of this plane may perceive us."]=7,
  ["Alas, I have prattled on long enough. Seek out my apprentice Ayessa Dawnsinger in the port of Valanaar if you find yourself out that way. She still hears the song--if only faintly. I am old and much of my power has left me. Ayessa represents the future of our people and the path we must now walk to survive. It's up to her and young skyborne such as yourself to carry the hopes for our people forward."]=8,
},
[251903]={ -- Rathiril Sunlance
  ["Hello there, young mage. I am Rathiril Sunlance and I am an elder Magister of the High Order here on Zephras Isle. It's always good to see bright-eyed young shen'dorei, ready to do their duty in service to their homeland. Don't let this dusty old mage hold you up however, no doubt you've got many adventures to see to. Feel free to stop by later if you'd like to speak more."]=1,
  ["Hello there, young $c. I am Rathiril Sunlance and I am an elder Magister of the High Order here on Zephras Isle. It's always good to see bright-eyed young shen'dorei, ready to do their duty in service to their homeland. Don't let this dusty old mage hold you up however, no doubt you've got many adventures to see to. Feel free to stop by later if you'd like to speak more."]=1,
  ["Where to begin? Our home is failing. The wards have fallen and the three provinces have begun to drift apart. There was a time not long ago when the spires of Shen'dramar were visible from the western watchtower. No longer. Day by day the wind pylons that anchor our home to this plane weaken..."]=2,
  ["Why is this happening? Put simply, the spirits of the wind just... vanished. The petty sprites and lesser elementals you've likely encountered out there are a pale imitation of the true spirits of wind. Non-sentient, aimless, and a far cry from the kindly spirits we lived in harmony alongside for thousands of years."]=3,
  ["Many disagree on this point. The Windshapers would have you believe that joining hands and merely hoping for the spirits' return will be sufficient. Their order's power has waned however, and their path relies on putting us back on the cycle of dependence that got us to this point. The High Order on the other hand... we believe in a more direct approach."]=4,
  ["The Cult? They are zealots and killers. They believe that we are being punished for some unspecific sin. The reality is that those that lead them are opportunists leftover from a dubious order of so-called 'Priests' of Al'Akir, the Windlord. They now find themselves in a position to weaponize the fear of our people to consolidate their own power... and they have been quick to do so."]=5,
  ["Even the Windshapers would tell you that the spirits never spoke highly of any supreme being amongst them. They acknowledged the existence of a being named Al'Akir, but they avoided invoking his name, almost as if they feared him. Even if this Al'Akir is an all-powerful 'Windlord' or ruler of the wind elementals, relying upon elementals is what got us into this mess. We must now see ourselves out of it."]=6,
  ["You must remember that while this realm has been our home for millennia, we will always be somewhat alien to this place. We are not in the terrestrial world that birthed our people. We are in the realm of Skywall, the elemental plane of air. We arrived here as the guests of spirits with whom we found kinship in ages past. Now that we Shen'dorei find ourselves bereft of their presence--and potentially--their protection, there's no telling how the other denizens of this plane may perceive us."]=7,
  ["Alas, I have prattled on long enough. Should you find yourself in the port of Valanaar, seek out Elaadrin Evengale. Elaadrin was once my student, but now he serves as the Chief Magister of the High Order. He is headstrong and capable, and it's now up to him and young Skyborne such as yourself to carry the hopes for our people forward."]=8,
},
[251904]={ -- Sania Silverstream
  ["Greetings, $c. Do you come seeking the blessings of the Windlord?"]=1,
  ["Greetings, rogue. Do you come seeking the blessings of the Windlord?"]=1,
},
[251905]={ -- Zerril Softbreeze
  ["If you need training as a cook, I have a few tips and tricks I could pass on! Ho ho! Throw on an apron and let's get started!"]=1,
  ["Ho there, traveler! New to town? Well, once you get settled in come see me if you'd like some work. I've been working overtime preparing for the Festival of Winds and I'll take all the help I can get keeping the larders full!"]=2,
},
[251906]={ -- Teeri Wellwind
  ["Unless you are here on business pertaining to V.L.O., I'm afraid I won't have a lot of time for chatter. If you want to pitch in and help out around town, I'll certainly put you to work though. Oh, what does V.L.O. stand for? Village Live Operations, of course. Even frontier towns like these don't manage themselves. Between major incidents, unplanned wind power outages, and bug infestations, keeping this place moving forward is no joke."]=1,
},
[251913]={ -- Aedi Thriceforged
  ["I can teach you to swing a blacksmith's hammer, if you are willing to learn."]=1,
},
[251968]={ -- Ayessa Dawnsinger
  ["<Ayessa Dawnsinger eyes you with barely-contained fury.> You are either very bold, or very stupid to so brazenly step foot into our domain after spilling Windshaper blood. We are slow to forgive, and we never forget. You should remove yourself from here at once. If we weren't in the center of Zephras, you would already be dead."]=1,
  ["Hmm, I see. Very well then, mage. The Windshapers will provide aid. Please inform Valennia that she can count on us for this fight. <Ayessa lowers her voice dangerously.> Do not mistake our cooperation for any sort of forgiveness. You owe the Windshapers blood, and someday we will collect."]=2,
  ["Hmm, I see. Very well then, $c. The Windshapers will provide aid. Please inform Valennia that she can count on us for this fight. <Ayessa lowers her voice dangerously.> Do not mistake our cooperation for any sort of forgiveness. You owe the Windshapers blood, and someday we will collect."]=2,
  ["Greetings, I am Ayessa Dawnsinger, the current Grand Skyseer of the Windshapers. What may I do for you?"]=3,
  ["If the High Order gave any mind at all to actually solving the problems we face and spent less time obsessing over the old magic, we'd be in a far better position as a people. It was Highborne magic that brought about the ruin of the kaldorei to begin with. Those self-absorbed fools seek to repeat those mistakes! The fact that they attempted to make peace with the cult is bad enough, but spilling Windshaper blood is what is truly unforgivable. Were it not for the imminent threat of the cult, I'd gather up our forces and go put an end to Elaadrin and the High Order once and for all."]=4,
  ["Hmm, I see. Very well then, $c. The Windshapers will provide aid. Please inform Valennia that she can count on us for this fight."]=5,
},
[251991]={ -- Taleen Shimmerthread
  ["The clothcraft of the Shen'dorei is a harmonious imitation of the flowing, carefree currents of the winds. While the spirits have left us, and I know not when I may see them dance once more... I find great comfort in my art, if only as a distraction. I can teach you to work the cloth as well, if you'd like to learn?"]=1,
},
[251992]={ -- Fenn Fairweather
  ["Welcome to Shen'dar Village, some of the best fishing this side of the mountain range. If you are looking to catch fish I can teach you, for a price."]=1,
},
[251993]={ -- Indari Sunseam
  ["I can teach you to craft fine leather armor, if you have the aptitude."]=1,
},
[252019]={ -- Abra Cadabra
  ["How may I help you today?"]=1,
},
[252068]={ -- Al'Aketh Stormcaller
  ["Soon all Shen'dorei will see the truth... and those that refuse will be swept away in the coming storm!"]=1,
  ["Why are you bothering me, recruit? If you want to talk to other doe-eyed fools, try the inn on the north side of town. The recruits that congregate there tend to have brains as smooth as their freshly shaved heads. Oh, and shave that head of yours. The only thing the windlord abhors more than chatty recruits is chatty recruits with a full head of hair. Now, be gone from my sight."]=2,
},
[252085]={ -- Archmage Celindra
  ["Yes? I am quite busy."]=1,
},
[252155]={ -- Peacekeeper Vaaniel
  ["<The corpse lying before you is covered in scorches and burn marks. He seems to be clutching something in his hand.>"]=1,
},
[252312]={ -- Second Chair Pawdo
  ["Hello! Frederick's Fabulous Furniture, Pawdo speaking."]=1,
},
[252359]={ -- Lotheluum Starbreeze
  ["Our kind are rare these days, but there are those who still dream in emerald amongst the Shen'dorei."]=1,
},
[252373]={ -- Anathamaas Aetherwind
  ["The followers of the old Highborne ways have never been more hungry for knowledge and to reclaim what we've lost. If you would seek to wield the power of the arcane and have the aptitude, I can help you take your next steps."]=1,
},
[252376]={ -- Emerii Tallgust
  ["Do you seek training as a leatherworker?"]=1,
},
[252378]={ -- Yorana Windyreed
  ["Storms curse these Al'Aketh fanatics!"]=1,
},
[252379]={ -- Eltheen Nightbreeze
  ["Slay your enemies and swoon your paramours with this one weird trick. If you follow the path of the rogue, I can teach you... for a cost, of course."]=1,
},
[252380]={ -- Othesia Evengale
  ["Welcome to my shop, it's good to see another Tailor here in Valanaar. Are you here for a lesson perhaps?"]=1,
},
[252382]={ -- Sessaria Skystride
  ["The spirits of the wind may have left us, but the power of the elements is not entirely out of reach for those with the patience to seek them out. If you are initiated in the ways of the shaman, I can help you grasp them."]=1,
},
[252383]={ -- Valennia Stormfist
  ["Greetings, citizen."]=1,
  ["I suppose that is true. I and the rest of my elites used to belong to an order known as the Empyrean Blades. We were the personal guard of our former leader, the Shal'nan. In the current, uncertain times we do what we can to help lead the peacekeepers citizen militia, since we are the closest thing to professional soldiers left on Zephras."]=2,
  ["<Valenna looks away briefly before looking hesitantly back in your direction.> The Shal'nan was the very best of us. It was he who stood up for our people against madness and oppression in Eldre'Thalas nearly ten thousand years ago. It was the Shal'nan who led us across the uncharted sea to escape the murderous vengeance of our ancient enemies. It was the Shal'nan who brokered the pact of friendship with the wind spirits that allowed us to ascend to Skywall... and survive. He was ever the servant leader to his people, even after he abdicated his position of power and retired."]=3,
  ["Valennia looks away briefly before looking hesitantly back in your direction. The Shal'nan was the very best of us. It was he who stood up for our people against madness and oppression in Eldre'Thalas nearly ten thousand years ago. It was the Shal'nan who led us across the uncharted sea to escape the murderous vengeance of our ancient enemies. It was the Shal'nan who brokered the pact of friendship with the wind spirits that allowed us to ascend to Skywall... and survive. He was ever the servant leader to his people, even after he abdicated his position of power and retired."]=3,
  ["I might be the only living shen'dorei left amongst our people who had more than a handful of words with him. I served him as the captain of his Empyrean Blades for nearly nine centuries, right up until... he left us. Even still, I can't rightly claim that I 'knew' him. He was ever a reserved and solitary man. He spent most of his time alone or in communion with the spirits in the spires high above the Shrine of the Four Winds... the place that the cult now calls the 'Shrine of Akir'."]=4,
  ["If I knew that then I suspect that life here on Zephras would be much, much easier. So many of our struggles and conflicts revolve around that very mystery. I appreciate your curiosity on this matter but I'm afraid that is all I have to say about this for today."]=5,
  ["The Peacekeepers can't hope to muster the numbers needed for an outright assault on the shrine. Without the Windshapers and the High Order bolstering our numbers, we stand no chance. They both pledged their aid when we need it. Now is the time. Unfortunately some recent events have led to outright bloodshed between the two factions, and tensions are high. How do you feel about a bit of diplomacy?"]=6,
},
[252388]={ -- Halavuul Cragwind
  ["You might think that just because we live on a floating island, there would be no need for miners like me. After so many thousands of years however, we still manage to dig up a lot of interesting things. It's almost like there's some invisible force, constantly creating new mineral deposits every so often. That's magic for you though, right? Regardless, if you need training as a miner them I'm your shen'dorei."]=1,
  ["You might think that just because we live on a floating island, there would be no need for miners like me. After so many thousands of years, however, we still manage to dig up a lot of interesting things. It's almost like there's some invisible force, constantly creating new mineral deposits every so often. That's magic for you though, right? Regardless, if you need training as a miner, then I'm your shen'dorei."]=2,
},
[252392]={ -- Orsaan Dalewind
  ["Greetings, young mage. Welcome to the hall of the Tradesman's Guild. Resources are tight on Zephras right now, but you should be able to find a variety of materials and wares here to keep you in top adventuring form. Please let me know if you have any questions."]=1,
  ["Greetings, young $c. Welcome to the hall of the Tradesman's Guild. Resources are tight on Zephras right now, but you should be able to find a variety of materials and wares here to keep you in top adventuring form. Please let me know if you have any questions."]=1,
},
[252448]={ -- Alvarion Windfield
  ["<The man lying before you shifts uncomfortably. He's recovering from some very nasty wounds.>"]=1,
  ["It's always great to see you, adventurer."]=2,
  ["Hmm, what an odd question? Not much, I suppose. My mother used to use it as a powder for babies to prevent diaper rash, but past that, I don't know of any other good use for it. Why do you ask?"]=3,
},
[252475]={ -- Elaadrin Evengale
  ["Greetings, I am Elaadrin Evengale, the current Supreme Magister of the High Order. How can I help you?"]=1,
  ["The Windshapers are almost wholly to blame for everything that has happened. Their refusal to change has damaged our ability to save ourselves from our current peril. They speak in absolutes and treat assumptions and superstitious hope as fact. Do you know who else deals only absolutes? The Al'Aketh. I for one do not intend to let blind adherence to dangerous beliefs doom our people. If it weren't for the threat of the cult, I'd march our mages over to the other side of Valnaar and wipe the Windshapers out."]=2,
  ["I see. This seems dangerous in the extreme, but the situation seems to demand that risks be taken. Very well, the High Order will provide aid. Please inform Valennia that she can count on us for this fight."]=3,
  ["Elaadrin eyes you with barely-contained hatred. You would dare step foot into our sanctum after spilling High Order blood? You are very brave, or very stupid. The High Order does not forgive, nor do we forget. Someday, you will pay for your crimes in blood."]=4,
  ["Hmm, I see. Very well then, $c. The High Order will assist the Peacekeepers. Please inform Valennia that she can count on us for this fight. <Elaadrin lowers his voice dangerously.> Do not mistake our willing cooperation for any sort of clemency. You owe the High Order blood, and we always collect on our debts."]=5,
},
[252476]={ -- Talaanis Shadowsong
  ["Welcome to Valanaar, mage."]=1,
  ["Welcome to Valanaar, $c."]=1,
  ["It is vital that we learn more about what the cult is planning, and with the turncoat dead the information may have died with him..."]=2,
},
[252477]={ -- Peacekeeper Elite
  ["May I help you locate something, citizen?"]=1,
  ["The bank and auction house can be found on the western side of Valanaar, near the Windshapers' skycutter dock."]=2,
  ["Greetings, citizen."]=3,
  ["Which class trainer are you looking for?"]=4,
  ["You'll find Lotheluum Starbreeze on a cliff overlooking the waterfall on the eastern edge of town."]=5,
},
[252478]={ -- Xy'aaria Streamrunner
  ["The skycutters and ferries haven't run in years at this point. For all we know, there are no other islands left for us to get imports from. Still though, I'm here... just in case."]=1,
},
[252479]={ -- Daeann Steelwind
  ["Ah, hello. You look as though you have a question for me."]=1,
  ["I hope that your interruption is for a good cause, I was in the middle of some important work."]=2,
},
[252500]={ -- Ranger Telenus
  ["Train a dog, I said. How hard could it be, I said. I need to stop talking."]=1,
},
[252800]={ -- Aamelia Windfield
  ["The Windfield Orchard has seen better days..."]=1,
  ["Thank you for your help. Make sure you let my husband know that the farm is safe."]=2,
},
[253002]={ -- Fillion Flamebreeze
  ["<The Skyborne lying before you is unconscious.>"]=1,
},
[253004]={ -- Iaadaria Bitterwind
  ["I hope that your interruption is for a good cause, I was in the middle of some important work."]=1,
  ["Gales greetings, friend. Is there something I can help you with?"]=2,
  ["Winds tidings. What can I help you with?"]=3,
  ["Ah, hello. You look as though you have a question for me."]=4,
},
[253092]={ -- Alba Fairmoon
  ["I am told the farms of Westfall once supplied a bounty of crops for Stormwind. But now, the soil is barren and most of the farmers have fled. On behalf of Darnassus I would like to offer my aid in replenishing this land. Will you assist me?"]=1,
},
[253183]={ -- Chatty Contender
  ["Oh, greetings rogue. Didn't see you there. Not that it matters but how long have you been listening?"]=1,
},
[253372]={ -- Dead Cultist
  ["<This cultist is dead. Upon close inspection, you notice that he seems to be clutching something to his chest, almost as if he was protecting it.>"]=1,
},
[253474]={ -- Peacekeeper
  ["Greetings, citizen."]=1,
  ["The bank and auction house can be found on the western side of Valanaar, near the Windshapers' skycutter dock."]=2,
  ["May I help you locate something, citizen?"]=3,
  ["A mailbox can be located just outside of the Inn, near the road leading north out of town."]=4,
  ["What are you looking for, citizen?"]=5,
  ["Which class trainer are you looking for?"]=6,
  ["The mage trainer can be found over in the High Order's lodge, on the southeastern edge of town."]=7,
  ["Which profession?"]=8,
  ["That trainer can be found in a house near the High Order dock, on the southeastern edge of town."]=9,
  ["You'll find Lotheluum Starbreeze on a cliff overlooking the waterfall on the eastern edge of town."]=10,
  ["Is there something I can help you find?"]=11,
},
[253514]={ -- Orweyna
  ["Zul'jarra should know the history we saw with Zul'jan in the Den of Echoes. That's what he's doing all of this for. Because of what I showed him..."]=1,
},
[253515]={ -- Captain Tokka
  ["When we first wrecked on this island, I set my crew to explore. Look for supplies, allies, the like. I can tell ya what we know."]=1,
},
[253576]={ -- Hyusaa Quickbreeze
  ["Most of the cultists at the Sanctum of Storms seem to have come out to respond to our attack. I never would have expected this to go so well. This was almost too easy... I think that the Windshapers and High Order have made their push. Valennia should be with them. You should head inside and find her. We'll stay here and keep watch while Valennia and the others finish what they came here to do."]=1,
},
[253590]={ -- Valennia Stormfist
  ["<Valennia is severely wounded and is barely holding on to consciousness.>"]=1,
},
[253837]={ -- Apothecary Dezi
  ["Mmm... you look troubled. Headaches? Curses? Or just bad decisions? I treat all three, sometimes the same way."]=1,
},
[253844]={ -- Valennia Stormfist
  ["Greetings, citizen."]=1,
},
[253847]={ -- Elaadrin Evengale
  ["Lorthuna is performing some sort of ritual up there. She may be trying to bring down the wards! The help we sent for has not yet arrived, but we'll just have to manage with what we have. When you are ready, let me know and we'll go confront her."]=1,
},
[253849]={ -- Ayessa Dawnsinger
  ["Lorthuna is performing some sort of ritual up there. She may be trying to bring down the wards! The help we sent for has not yet arrived, but we'll just have to manage with what we have. When you are ready, let me know and we'll go confront her."]=1,
},
[254086]={ -- Shenaan Spellwind
  ["The followers of the old Highborne ways have never been more hungry for knowledge and to reclaim what we've lost. If you would seek to wield the power of the arcane and have the aptitude, I can help you take your next steps."]=1,
},
[254087]={ -- Miriaan Mistblade
  ["Slay your enemies and swoon your paramours with this one weird trick. If you follow the path of the rogue, I can teach you... for a cost, of course."]=1,
},
[254089]={ -- Coriella Calmbreeze
  ["Welcome to the Calmbreeze Inn, traveler. Would you like some refreshment?"]=1,
},
[254100]={ -- Zephras Citizen
  ["If the Al'Aketh cult isn't stopped soon, we'll all be press-ganged into joining those fanatics. I will NOT look good with a shaved head."]=1,
  ["Have you heard of what's become of Ban'aethal? The peacekeepers are warning people to stay away from the ruins and the Shadowgale Forest entirely. I overheard someone at the inn talking about seeing malevolent wind spirits that seemed to be little more than a hazy outline, as if they were... hollowed out somehow. Gives me the chills just thinking about such a thing."]=2,
  ["Have you seen them? The skycutters are running again! I've heard that we still have no contact with the other shen'dorei islands, though. I hope we re-establish contact with Shen'dramar and Eldranaar soon... if they are even still out there."]=3,
  ["The Al'Aketh cult claims that Al'Akir the 'Windlord' will save us from our current woes here on Zephras. If Al'Akir is real and really is the ruler of Skywall, why did the wind spirits refuse to speak of him for so long? Either he isn't real, or even worse, he's real and he's not as benevolent as the cult claims him to be. Either way, nothing about what the cult is doing is good for us normal folk."]=4,
  ["I've seen the skycutters sailing through the sky more and more recently. It's good to know that they are running again. If only the elders would tell us what is going on. They only tell us that nothing has changed and we still have no contact with the other islands. I can't help but wonder what this means..."]=5,
},
[254128]={ -- Wardrobe
  ["<The two cultists nearby are talking. You might be able to learn something if you hide behind this wardrobe and eavesdrop.>"]=1,
},
[254149]={ -- Sirocca "Swimmers" Starfeather
  ["The skyborne before you sways unsteadily, clearly very inebriated. I used to be a sailor you know? Before the trouble started. The skycutters used to run between the islands. Now its unsafe or some such, or so they say. I see the High Order and the Windshapers have their skycutters running again, but I'm stuck here, grounded! What aren't we being told! He turns and yells loudly at the innkeeper. WHAT AREN'T WE BEING TOLD, DONAAL!?"]=1,
  ["Shadowgale Forest! It's haunted! Haunted as the sky is blue! Terrible forest spirits, terror birds with talons as big as yer arm! It's... a nightmare! Swimmers turns to Donaal and belches loudly. IT'S NOT CRAZY TALK, DONAAL!"]=2,
},
[254151]={ -- Vayn Moongaze
  ["The Nightclaw do not take kindly to reckless intruders. Tread carefully while in Shadowgale, mage."]=1,
  ["The Nightclaw do not take kindly to reckless intruders. Tread carefully while in Shadowgale, $c."]=1,
  ["You've earned a degree of trust amongst the Nightclaw, mage. We don't have much to offer you as a reward, but we have managed to scavenge a number of crafting plans from the ruins of Ban'aethal. The magesmiths of Ban'aethal were widely regarded to be the best artisans in all of the Skyborne Isles. The Nightclaw are naturalists, not crafters, so these records are of little use to us. Continue to prove yourself to be a valuable ally, and I would make these secrets available to you."]=2,
  ["You've earned a degree of trust amongst the Nightclaw, $c. We don't have much to offer you as a reward, but we have managed to scavenge a number of crafting plans from the ruins of Ban'aethal. The magesmiths of Ban'aethal were widely regarded to be the best artisans in all of the Skyborne Isles. The Nightclaw are naturalists, not crafters, so these records are of little use to us. Continue to prove yourself to be a valuable ally, and I would make these secrets available to you."]=2,
},
[254345]={ -- Syriel Nightrain
  ["Gales greetings, friend. Is there something I can help you with?"]=1,
  ["Nostyec Regenthor, mod. E wirsh ador eynes re an tiras an lo vil va novaedi E gol melka ras re y bor rothas aelgestron."]=2,
},
[254565]={ -- Delver's Guide
  ["This book contains all the information documented on delves and delve-related things."]=1,
},
[255104]={ -- Jorvan Longmoor
  ["Good day. Can I help you? Maybe you'd like to take a look at some plans for artisanal rooms?"]=1,
  ["Always looking for work, if there's work to be had. And it seems you've done your part, so now we'll do ours. Just say the word, and I'll put the boys to the task."]=2,
  ["Unfortunately, I don't think you're quite ready for an upgrade. It's important to really get to know a house before you go making big changes. When you're truly ready to take things to the next level, we'll be here ready to make sure everything is plumb... and level."]=3,
},
[255222]={ -- "High Tides" Ren
  ["Hello, my friend. You looking for something rare? My friends and I, we travel. We bring you the fruits of those travels."]=1,
},
[255473]={ -- Maren Silverwing
  ["Welcome, adventurer! Have you been aiding in the defense of Quel'Thalas against the recent incursions? I'd be happy to exchange your hard-earned Field Accolades for the new weapons and armor we've recently discovered. I'm also happy to exchange any Dark Particles you may find during these incursions for Field Accolades. My sister and the other ren'dorei are studying them in hopes of better understanding who and where these attacks are coming from."]=1,
  ["After Xal'atath's initial attack on the Sunwell, a hidden cache of armor and weapons was discovered in the wreckage. We believe some of these may have been stashed here since the Legion's takeover of the Sunwell Plateau. It took us a bit to catalogue and check for any unsafe anomalies that may have formed during the years they were hidden, but we've managed to sort through them all. With more volunteers joining the Ranger Captain's strike force, we're going to need all the weapons and armor we can get."]=2,
  ["<Maren glances at Mayven before looking back at you with a smile.> Yes. Twin sister, in fact. We both shared a common fondness for magic, which led us to pursue further studies within the Magister's Terrace. I went down one path... and she went down another. It's been a few years since our fallout, but I'm grateful she's back. She's may be a bit... cold sometimes but she's harmless. Well, mostly. <Maren scrunches her nose as if doubting her own words.>"]=3,
},
[255476]={ -- Triam Dawnsetter
  ["This is such an interesting find!"]=1,
  ["A small group of us have been studying some relics from the recent assault on the city. The items appear to have been infused with latent void magic, which I believe has greatly increased their potential. The items' physical properties have also been altered, giving them all a striking look! Interesting, isn't it? Once we are sure they pose no threat to our own, we can start outfitting our troops with them and use this power against our enemies!"]=2,
},
[255479]={ -- Examiner Andoren Dawnrise
  ["Oh don't tell me you're also here to side with Lady Darkglen, Priest ?"]=1,
  ["On her approach to... everything! Studying historical sites, investigating strange magic, and even preserving relics of power! 'Lady' Darkglen isn't so much keen to preserve our history as she is to understand the darkness that threatens it. Even if that means taking a more destructive approach."]=2,
  ["Of course we should but at what cost? There must be a way to both preserve what is ours and defeat the enemies at our doorstep. We can do both, despite what Lady Darkglen thinks. Her obsession with dark powers has shattered her once-delicate approach to such things."]=3,
},
[255495]={ -- Rae'ana
  ["Greetings, human."]=1,
  ["The Ranger Captain acknowledges that my experience in relic study will be invaluable against the host of threats in the days ahead. Before this, I was cataloging relics for the Dragonscale Expedition. When our camp heard of the attack on the Sunwell, I joined those who raced to return home to Silvermoon. I have not forgotten when the people of Quel'Thalas rallied to defend Suramar years ago. I will help in any way I can."]=2,
},
[255499]={ -- Ji-eun
  ["Oh, hello there!"]=1,
  ["Young... I was the oldest Explorer-In-Training at the basecamp! Plus I had been starting to work with Rae'ana studying artifacts. She agreed to take me on as an apprentice. I have never been to a city like Silvermoon. It is so grand! We got to visit Valdrakken once, but there are so many more people here."]=2,
},
[255503]={ -- Sergeant Vornin
  ["Please be quick--I have a lot to do."]=1,
},
[255853]={ -- Urs'endris
  ["The spirit of strength does not always allude to physical strength. To face adversity both from within and without is what it means to take my shape."]=1,
},
[255940]={ -- Donaal Downbreeze
  ["Welcome to the Calmbreeze Inn, traveler. Would you like some refreshment?"]=1,
},
[256078]={ -- Lyssabel Dawnpetal
  ["Hello! I would be happy to help you with your housing needs."]=1,
},
[256083]={ -- Riaani Nightwind
  ["Riaani seems to be intently focused on his work on the wind construct."]=1,
  ["Have you found what we need yet?"]=2,
},
[256247]={ -- Belathaan Brightwish
  ["What are you doing here? Quickly, leave this place now. You are going to ruin everything!"]=1,
},
[256252]={ -- Whispering Winds
  ["The spinning column of wind before you seems to hum with contentment. It clearly cannot speak, but you have a clear sense of the sensations it feels. It seems... happy to provide you with the blessing of the winds."]=1,
},
[256306]={ -- Arcanist Laurain
  ["Welcome to Dalaran, mage. Please pay no mind to some of the construction that is still underway. Oh, and should you encounter a rogue arcane anomaly, demon, or other malign entity, please feel free to seek the assistance from the nearest member of the Kirin Tor before fleeing--um... proceeding--to the nearest exit in an orderly fashion! <Arcanist Laurain laughs nervously.> Thank you for visiting!"]=1,
},
[256386]={ -- Dokimi
  ["We've had trouble with shipments going missing across Azeroth. If you find any, I'd appreciate if you could return them to me."]=1,
},
[256388]={ -- Jornah
  ["Greetings and well met, adventurer! Your arrival is timely, and we here at the Durotar Supply and Logistics company are always in need of new contractors. If you are someone with a knack for gathering useful materials or the skills to craft something from scratch, you have a place here. Please let me know if you have any questions."]=1,
  ["Recently there has been a sharp rise in lost orders. We strive to ensure that each delivery is efficient and safe, but with a rise of bandits, rowdy creatures, and those damned Alliance, inevitably not every delivery goes according to plan. Should you find these shipments, take a look over the label for what it should contain. It is not your responsibility to deal with our mistakes, but if you complete the shipment, you will be rewarded in kind. Dokimi over by the wagon can handle the logistics and your compensation. We will take it from there."]=2,
  ["I am glad you asked! We are far more than just a delivery service, adventurer. We employ and contract craftsman across a variety of specialties and trades, and keep our ear to the ground for any new opportunities to keep their hands busy and goods flowing. We cannot possibly predict the emergent needs of any potential client, so we depend on their crafting orders to arrive to us. You can imagine that this pipeline is... not as effective as we would hope. We encourage any crafters to satisfy these demands and deliver the goods directly to the customers, wherever they may be. Worry not, you will be fairly compensated for your troubles and earn respect among our organization."]=3,
  ["Yes! Well. Sort of. Gold is the true universal currency, but we have our own system for trade amongst ourselves known as Merchant's Favor. It abstracts away the ever-fluctuating value of gold and silver, and ensures fair and equitable trade between members of the organization. It cannot be liquidated to gold, unless you're engaging in some shady activity, I suppose. We still use gold for typical day-to-day needs such as materials needed for common crafts, but otherwise rely on Merchant's Favor for any kind of internal commerce. If you assist us with recovering waylaid crates and ensuring swift fulfillment of craftsman's writs, you will earn plenty!"]=4,
},
[256390]={ -- Marcy Baker
  ["We've had trouble with shipments going missing across Azeroth. If you find any, I'd appreciate if you could return them to me."]=1,
},
[256635]={ -- Peacekeeper
  ["Adventurer! The wind bridge leading to the other spire is unstable. You may need to wait here with me until it returns."]=1,
},
[256734]={ -- Daniel Stitchsong
  ["Hello there! I've got the finest leathers this side of Stormwind. Interested?"]=1,
},
[256735]={ -- Mivin Shadowweave
  ["<Mivin gestures toward his wares and back at you again with a smile, but says nothing.>"]=1,
},
[257003]={ -- Ishlee Breezewhisper
  ["Gales greetings, friend. Is there something I can help you with?"]=1,
  ["I hope that your interruption is for a good cause, I was in the middle of some important work."]=2,
  ["I don't get too many Skinners in here looking for training, but I guess I could teach you something if you're ready."]=3,
},
[257004]={ -- Eaysaa Brightgust
  ["Welcome to my shop, it's good to see another Enchanter here in Valanaar. Are you here for a lesson perhaps?"]=1,
},
[257005]={ -- Valiena Swiftgale
  ["I hope that your interruption is for a good cause, I was in the middle of some important work."]=1,
  ["Winds tidings. What can I help you with?"]=2,
  ["Nostyec Aetwinter, mod. E wirsh ador eynes re an tiras an lo vil va novaedi E gol melka ras re y bor rothas aelgestron."]=3,
},
[257006]={ -- Nyalah Brightfire
  ["I don't get too many cooks in here looking for training, but I guess I could teach you something if you're ready."]=1,
  ["E borne hir ash nuff garde re ruff vassild lon thorniss, far E regen E majis barad ras aetwinter lo ruftos ergin."]=2,
},
[257007]={ -- Melasa Fairmend
  ["Va, y ealdor Gloinador. E majis ko dana ne barad ras thorniss lars majis gol ador endirvis."]=1,
  ["I hope that your interruption is for a good cause. I was in the middle of some important work."]=2,
  ["Oh, a fellow Physician. I would be glad to teach you anything that would aid your journeys."]=3,
},
[257008]={ -- Baelann Swiftcurrent
  ["Re, y ealdor Regenthor. Hir ras novaedi re uden va y vandar thorniss? Melka E gol ruff ras y garde va vil?"]=1,
  ["I hope that your interruption is for a good cause, I was in the middle of some important work."]=2,
  ["Ah, a fellow Fisherman. Are you perhaps in need of a little training? Maybe I can show you a thing or two?"]=3,
},
[257018]={ -- Naleeia Tattermend
  ["Gales greetings, friend. Is there something I can help you with?"]=1,
  ["Va, y ealdor Gloinador. E majis ko dana ne barad ras thorniss lars majis gol ador endirvis."]=2,
},
[257019]={ -- Nyassa Swiftdraught
  ["Winds tidings. What can I help you with?"]=1,
  ["Nostyec Aetwinter, mod. E wirsh ador eynes re an tiras an lo vil va novaedi E gol melka ras re y bor rothas aelgestron."]=2,
},
[257020]={ -- Nasalanna Windsinger
  ["Welcome to my shop, it's good to see another Enchanter here in Shen'dar. Are you here for a lesson perhaps?"]=1,
},
[257021]={ -- Halassa Fernbreeze
  ["Nostyec Regenthor, mod. E wirsh ador eynes re an tiras an lo vil va novaedi E gol melka ras re y bor rothas aelgestron."]=1,
},
[257022]={ -- Messana Crestwind
  ["You might think that just because we live on a floating island, there would be no need for miners like me. After so many thousands of years however, we still manage to dig up a lot of interesting things. It's almost like there's some invisible force, constantly creating new mineral deposits every so often. That's magic for you though, right? Regardless, if you need training as a miner them I'm your shen'dorei."]=1,
},
[257036]={ -- Baelann Favorbreeze
  ["Welcome to the Bank of Valanaar. We can secure your belongings and valuables here should you so desire. Do you wish to access your deposit box?"]=1,
},
[257065]={ -- Missionary Jasaan
  ["Do you seek the blessings of the Windlord?"]=1,
},
[257298]={ -- Loa Speaker Yl'mul
  ["All that's left here is me and de captain. De curse I cast keeps us from movin' on."]=1,
},
[257321]={ -- Fel'orei Moonstrider
  ["Welcome. I offer some of the finest goods imported from the human lands of Westfall."]=1,
},
[257411]={ -- Ranger Captain Lilatha
  ["The threats that lay siege to Eversong and Zul'Aman's borders are relentless, adventurer, but we are no strangers to dealing with these attacks. Be it forces of the Void, marauding ethereals, or the Twilight's Blade, we will be ready."]=1,
},
[257415]={ -- Kul'amara the Fierce
  ["I hope you're not wasting my time, human."]=1,
  ["My guards, ha. They are more accurately your guards. It is nice though dat they think three of dem are enough to stop me if I did want to do harm. Mibaza could take them alone. <Mibaza lets out a low growl.>"]=2,
  ["How many times must I repeat myself... De factions attacking your perfect elf allies are also attacking us in Zul'Aman. A few of you have proven worthy fighters and honorable enough we hope to work together to combat de new threats. Does dat satisfy your inquiry?"]=3,
},
[257416]={ -- Lady Darkglen
  ["<Lady Darkglen tilts her head as she looks you over.> Now, what can an important priest like yourself do for me?"]=1,
  ["<Lady Darkglen sighs.> Due to the current climate of Silvermoon, it was unwise to have my usual... entourage here in the city. While dear Blocciniux is away, I have an alternate. Do try to behave in front of him, hmm? He's quite dedicated to his job."]=2,
  ["A part of the Reliquary? Me? I'm afraid not. I've always found their work to be rather fascinating--I've even contributed to Tae'thelan's lavish fundraisers that finance his expeditions. But sadly, the High Examiner has never granted me membership. I must have offended him at some point. <Lady Darkglen offers a coy smirk.> And yet, when the need arose for someone with an intrigue for both dark magic and history alike, none were as suited to the task as I was. He couldn't deny my credentials, so in turn he sent Andoren here to lecture me on... well, I've stopped listening to his prattle if I'm being honest."]=3,
},
[257443]={ -- Darvan Darkdust
  ["These domanaar make for unlikely allies. Most were wronged by Xal'atath in some way, or have ambitions beyond what she has to offer. The enemy of my enemy, I suppose."]=1,
},
[257446]={ -- Teo Hammerstorm
  ["The stone an' soil speak truer than any tongue, if ye quiet the clatter in yer heart long enough to hear 'em. If ye've the makings of a shaman, I'll teach ye."]=1,
},
[257554]={ -- Halaan Hawk-Eye
  ["<The gaze of the ranger standing before you is fixed on the enormous anchor pylon in the distance.>"]=1,
},
[257655]={ -- Deathguard Billmuth
  ["<Deathguard Billmuth absentmindedly fidgets as he looks around nervously. He is clearly very uncomfortable being here.>"]=1,
},
[257703]={ -- Scout Adaephus
  ["I hope you didn't come alone. The host is pulling reinforcements from the Void faster than we can kill them. If we let this turn into a battle of attrition, we've already lost. Fortunately, their Summoning Pylons are fragile. Shatter them and send their forces back to the Void. Take my cloak, it will help you get close, maybe even get the drop on some of these fiends."]=1,
},
[257803]={ -- Tak'lejo
  ["My people, kidnapped! Stolen! Killed! Many more are missin'! And de hash'ey's brother walks free!"]=1,
  ["Ula'tek ain't a name I have heard before. If ya ask me to guess, it's a powerful serpent of some kind. A dead loa, maybe. Even when Zul'jin led de Amani, de only stories told of Atal'Utek were of a cursed temple built on a rocky sea. Exiles and criminals sometimes risked de boat ride here to escape Amani justice, never to be seen again."]=2,
},
[258043]={ -- Norric Lochthane
  ["Ye've come further than many, adventurer. Respect the elements around ye and ye shall fare far greater than most."]=1,
},
[258113]={ -- Ingrid Dunwald
  ["The spirits have guided you to me. How may I be of service?"]=1,
},
[258130]={ -- Jorel Windsinger
  ["<Before you lies the corpse Jorel Windsinger. Deep lacerations are cut into his legs, and lightning burns scorch his fur. It is clear he put up a fight before succombing to his wounds.>"]=1,
},
[258568]={ -- Antonio Bolero
  ["Best deals in all of Stormwind my friend, won't find any better. Now, what can I help you with?"]=1,
  ["Just browsing my wares or is there something specific I can help you find today?"]=2,
},
[258859]={ -- Zul'jarra
  ["The elves have refused me. I shouldn't be so surprised. I rely on you now more than ever, my hash'ura."]=1,
  ["I know de justice of Zul'Aman and how we deal with traitors. If he weren't my brother, I would take his head and paint my face with his blood for all he's done. But he is my brother. And I'm de hash'ey. Anyone who wants Jan gotta come through me first. Damn it, Jan... I know why he's doin' it. I just... <Zul'jarra winces and rubs the gash where Zul'jan cut her.> I'm de one who can knock some sense into him. I know there's a way."]=2,
},
[258860]={ -- Lady Liadrin
  ["Zul'jan gave her that wound? That traitorous little..."]=1,
},
[258930]={ -- Isaac Chan
  ["Ah friend, I only help hunters and their pets."]=1,
},
[259012]={ -- Ealaane Nimbuswalker
  ["All of the skyborne islands became destabilized and began to move apart a few years ago. If that wasn't bad enough, now large pieces of Zephras are beginning to fall away. It's hard to imagine your home falling into the sky, but that is my reality now."]=1,
},
[259013]={ -- Resaan Nimbuswalker
  ["<Before you lies an skyborne; his body is mangled and bruised but still recognizable. It is clear he met a gruesome end while attempting to flee. It appears that all of his belongings are still on his body, and a half filled crate nearby lays spilled on the ground.>"]=1,
},
[259084]={ -- Denaaris Stargale
  ["Wind's greetings, friend. I've been authorized to offer fellow Skyborne quick passage to the city of Stormwind. Please feel free to utilize this portal at your leisure."]=1,
},
[259118]={ -- Muln Earthfury
  ["I am Muln Earthfury of the Earthen Ring. What brings you before me today?"]=1,
},
[259190]={ -- Ephram Barbaro
  ["Oi, what do you want?"]=1,
},
[259644]={ -- Erus
  ["Erus scrap junk for you."]=1,
},
[260628]={ -- Valennia Stormfist
  ["Valennia winces in pain as she shifts to look at you. Don't look at me like that. I'll be fine. Despite the best efforts of the High Elder's fretful healers, I'll be up and ready to fight again in no time. Now be gone with you... don't let this old soldier hold you up. The winds will bring you good fortune on your journey, I know it."]=1,
},
[260638]={ -- Silvermoon Guard
  ["What do you seek, priest?"]=1,
},
[261472]={ -- Shadowguard Turncloak
  ["The ethereal says nothing as she stares out over the Voidstorm."]=1,
  ["Hal'hadar? How do you know that name? She takes the battery from you to examine it, holding it carefully as if not wanting to drop it. I do not know much about them. Even when I was a member of the Shadowguard, I rarely encountered them. The only Shadowguard who did were those with high enough clearance called in as security for their operations. All I know is that they were Sal'hadaar's research division. Where in the cosmos did you find this?"]=2,
  ["Leylines? They must be looking for a fuel source of some kind... As for the battery itself--do you see these argunite crystals inside the chassis and how they connect into this mainframe? There is no mistaking Lightforged technology. Weaving ethereal technomancy into other technologies is exactly what the Hal'hadar do. Perhaps one of the Lightforged draenei can tell you more about this. The ren'dorei mentioned that a few of them were stationed in the elven city of Silvermoon."]=3,
},
[261474]={ -- Ethereal Technomancer
  ["The ethereal is busy tinkering with something."]=1,
  ["Fascinating... I have never seen such an overlay of technology like this. This is no amateur work--whoever interlaced these together was both a skilled technomancer and quite familiar with Lightforged technology. There also appears to be a fine coating on the inner chassis... some sort of arcane conductor? It almost looks organic--spore-like even but...arcane charged? How curious..."]=2,
},
[261870]={ -- Captain Tokka
  ["It be good to see some fresh faces around here. My crew and I have been stranded for over seven years, and we were beginning to believe we'd have to rebuild society from scratch!"]=1,
  ["We'd been sailing Torga's Beak, a gift given to us by the Zandalari, when out of nowhere a great white serpent broke our hull. My crew acted quickly, and took us to shore before we took on too much water. Would have been better to let the ship sink and swim back to Zul'Aman, but little did we know the trap we had put ourselves in. After establishing ourselves on the island, we built small dinghies to escape--only to find the fogs constantly turning us back to shore. We've spent the last few years making this place a home. We had begun to acclimate, until just a day ago when the foul serpents poured forth from the mountainside. My crew scattered across this cursed island. What cruel winds, for the fog to lift only now."]=2,
  ["'Twas a cursed land, even before the snakes emerged. Many a crewmate found themselves attacked by the souls of the dead that wander here, and we've found a number of other Zandalari ships that met the fate of ours. To the north, we've made allies with a hermit by the name of Ofi, an Amani exile. She prefers to keep to herself, but is the only friendly face we've seen. To the east, the island turns to muck and mud, and a combination of murlocs and spirits make their home there. The murlocs have a crazed glint in their eyes... a curse that spread to some of my crewmates as well. As for the spirits, some of them seem friendly enough while others attack you on sight. We've generally found it best to avoid the dead."]=3,
  ["To the south lays Gnarldor Isle, where some burly giants seem to have taken home. They're none too friendly and we give them a wide berth. To the west are the crypts and temples where the snakes emerged from. My crew is a superstitious sort and don't like messing with graves, so we thought to leave the quiet lands alone. We didn't expect venom to spew from the mountains and flying snakes with two heads! You'd best be getting on with your soldiers. I could use your help around here later, but for now it seems we have an outpost to fortify. You're a ray of hope, adventurer."]=4,
  ["To the south lays Gnarldor Isle, where some burly giants seem to have taken home. They're none too friendly and we give them a wide berth. To the west are the crypts and temples where the snakes emerged from. My crew is a superstitious sort and don't like messing with graves, so we thought to leave the quiet lands alone. We didn't expect venom to spew from the mountains and flying snakes with two heads! You'd best be getting on with your soldiers. I could use your help around here later, but for now it seems we have an outpost to fortify. You're a ray of hope, Nerfwins."]=4,
},
[262204]={ -- Witherbark Cook
  ["The ingredients I've got are... suspicious at best. Eh, with your help I'm sure it'll be at least edible."]=1,
},
[262518]={ -- Wax Sculptor
  ["You have discerning eye. I can tell. Help me pick sculpture subject? Might need more wax. But BE WARNED! Wax art is temporary. No refunds when it melts."]=1,
  ["Too tired for new statue. Come back later. Unless you just want make this one bigger. Can do that easy. Just throw more wax. I sleep, you do."]=2,
},
[262560]={ -- Hana Lighthoof
  ["adventurer, how may I further your training in the eyes of the Earth Mother?"]=1,
},
[263113]={ -- Myriaal Mistwake
  ["It can get boring up here, you know. I can only annoy that stuffy wretch Halaan so much before even that gets old."]=1,
},
[263121]={ -- Mayven Ombrewing
  ["As you can no doubt tell, I am somewhat preoccupied with my research. Unless your question pertains to my work, please direct all matters to my sister, Maren."]=1,
  ["<Mayven closes her eyes as she slowly exhales before looking at you.> Yes, she is. If you're that curious about my familial relations, please feel free to ask her all about it. While you do that, I've got work that requires my attention. These dark particles aren't going to study themselves."]=2,
  ["<Mayven narrows her eyes at you for a moment before she gestures to the void magic circling around her hand.> Since you're so curious... I'm studying the dark particles left behind by these new threats. Why you may ask? Most types of magic leave behind a faint residue that can be used to determine the type of magic or in some cases, the reagents and fuel source used to power the spell. In this case, we are trying to unravel these particles to learn more about these threats and maybe find a way to counter their next move."]=3,
},
[263399]={ -- Sam Sarsaparilla
  ["Howdy there, traveler!"]=1,
},
[263479]={ -- Riftblade Maella
  ["The forces of the Void and the Hal'hadar are relentless in their onslaught. We must remain vigilant and ready."]=1,
},
[263664]={ -- Raan Wildwind
  ["Greetings, traveler."]=1,
},
[264009]={ -- Scally
  ["You wish to learn candlecraft? Fill up cauldron with wax. Can't teach without wax."]=1,
  ["Hmm, let me check ledger. In candle workshops, this town has made... 0 candles! Needs more. If you want expert opinion."]=2,
  ["Well and well and well, my friends! Big pot full and wax is hot. Is time to begin. Ready to learn?"]=3,
  ["Okay fine I tell you all steps. STEP ONE: fill candlepot with hot wax. Take from pile and bring near cauldron. Cauldron keeper will toss wax into pot. He very accurate. STEP TWO: put wick in the pot. We brought wick pile. Is tangled... untangle to find wicks. Put wick in full pot! STEP THREE: cool the pot. Wax still too hot at this stage. Need to cool down to make hard. Can just drop and wait or run it around to cool faster. STEP FOUR: pull out candle! Seem easy, but pot sometimes too tight. Ask friends to give a whack to loosen it up. Make at least one candle and workshop is success!"]=4,
  ["Wax is hot! Get to it! Okay fine I tell you all steps. STEP ONE: fill candlepot with hot wax. Take from pile and bring near cauldron. Cauldron keeper will toss wax into pot. He very accurate. STEP TWO: put wick in the pot. We brought wick pile. Is tangled... untangle to find wicks. Put wick in full pot! STEP THREE: cool the pot. Wax still too hot at this stage. Need to cool down to make hard. Can just drop and wait or run it around to cool faster. STEP FOUR: pull out candle! Seem easy, but pot sometimes too tight. Ask friends to give a whack to loosen it up. Make at least one candle and workshop is success!"]=5,
  ["Ooooh, teacher's pet, are you? Is good. I like animals. There only one secret to candlecraft. ... You listening?"]=6,
  ["Secret is teamwork. No tell. It don't matter who finishes candle long as candle is finished. We have quick kobold just catch wax. Smart kobold make wicks. Fast kobold cool pots. You see? Can pass pot between steps. Learned from earthen forgers. Is waste to make every kobold do every step."]=7,
  ["Hmm, let me check ledger. In candle workshops, this town has made... 4 candles! Needs more. If you want expert opinion."]=8,
  ["You think my time free? I have much business to attend as Best at Candlecraft. No need more time. Need get faster."]=9,
  ["Hmm, let me check ledger. In candle workshops, this town has made... 5 candles! Needs more. If you want expert opinion."]=10,
},
[264078]={ -- Sutara Plainstalker
  ["It is my honor to handle supply and provisioning for the Earthen Ring. My stock is limited at present, but check back with me often and I may have new equipment and supplies available for purchase."]=1,
},
[264337]={ -- Waxmonger Squick
  ["Nice place you have! Hear you need more candles. Now that I see, sad to say... is true. But we help. I brought our best at candlecraft. You learn, then won't need us!"]=1,
  ["First need wax. Everyone need wax. No take our wax, though. Find Home-Grown Wax in neighborhood. Wax everywhere if you know where to look. Our wax experts can help you use! Brought most talented sculptors. Give them some extra wax and they make art for you. Even brought tools to teach candlemaking! Will need to fill up cauldron to have enough for workshop. Then talk to Scally, our Best at Candlecraft. He run workshop. See how many candles your town can make! Have more wax than need? Seem impossible, but you can donate extra wax for neighbors at Neighborhood Wax chest. Can take some too if other neighbors donate. Go now! Much need doing."]=2,
},
[264936]={ -- Earthseer Farsen
  ["On a clear day, you can even see Blackrock Mountain from here. It's both beautiful and terrifying at the same time."]=1,
},
[265654]={ -- Faladriaal Featherfall
  ["Welcome to the guild registrar of Valanaar. How may I assist you today?"]=1,
},
[265809]={ -- Brakk
  ["Greetings, traveler."]=1,
},
[265811]={ -- Lyreena Duskblade
  ["Greetings, traveler."]=1,
},
[265812]={ -- Eleanor Shackleton
  ["Greetings, traveler."]=1,
},
[265813]={ -- Eric Brighthammer
  ["Greetings, traveler."]=1,
},
[265944]={ -- William Pickman
  ["Cooking is a life long pursuit and I see we share the same passion!"]=1,
  ["I can teach you how to cook!"]=2,
},
[266165]={ -- Sporomir
  ["Big problem! Huge problem! World ending problem! Need mighty heroes!"]=1,
  ["Rootways are for trees and haranir. No, we just rrr... Travel. Hard to explain. Like growing, but different."]=2,
},
[266484]={ -- Morbin Lightbane
  ["We paladins must earn our place amongst our Forsaken kin each day, lest we be judged as fanatics like the Scarlet Crusade. The light is not simply a tool of our foes, but a conduit for our righteous fury! It is in our devotion to the Dark Lady and the love of our home that we may channel the light to bring justice to our enemies. The Banshee Queen keeps a close eye on us. Let her. She will see that our resolve shall never waver. We are Forsaken!"]=1,
},
[266525]={ -- Sin'dorei Magister
  ["I knew I had a good reason to hate homework. My folio tried to fill my pack with mana cakes! And not even the good ones!"]=1,
},
[266526]={ -- Quel'dorei Magister
  ["I heard the ghost of Dar'Khan was spotted in the library! Is that true? Did he really try to blow up the Omnium?"]=1,
},
[266528]={ -- Ren'dorei Magister
  ["According to Veldharin, the first Seekers of Knowledge investigated the dark presence our ancestors felt in Tirisfal. No one knows specifically what they found, but apparently only a few of them returned with their minds intact. Whatever they saw or found was enough for Dath'Remar to outlaw void magic. Do you think Umbric has peered into it? Do you think we'll be allowed to?"]=1,
  ["I don't blame the Grand Magister for exiling those who followed Umbric. But I'll never forget the stares or the hatred in their faces. Years later, and some still bear the same expression... Isn't the pursuit of knowledge the entire point of this place?"]=2,
  ["It feels good to freely roam the Terrace again after all these years, despite the disapproval of some of the others. They can glower and frown all they want. It's not like we're going to exile them for expressing a difference of opinion..."]=3,
},
[267007]={ -- Stormwind Harbor Guard
  ["What do you need directions to?"]=1,
},
[267008]={ -- Leonid Barthalomew the Revered
  ["They named it Bandarion Keep. I wonder what Garek would make of that?"]=1,
},
[267009]={ -- Hadric Harlson
  ["Be careful, mage. There are cultists nearby."]=1,
  ["Be careful, $c. There are cultists nearby."]=1,
},
[267279]={ -- Cadoc Winterheart
  ["Hello, adventurer! Have you considered taking up a tradeskill? I would be happy to answer any questions you might have, or point you toward the local trainers. If this feels overwhelming, that's okay! You can always return here or visit trainers in capital cities to get started on your crafting journey at any time."]=1,
  ["Of course! Which profession would you like me to guide you towards? I will mark your map with the location of a local trainer of your choice. Remember that you can visit trainers in capital cities for more thorough training."]=2,
  ["Great choice. I have marked that location on your map."]=3,
},
[267324]={ -- Margaret Weaver
  ["Agol ne wirsh ver ne vandar novaedi veld algos nevren? Va se ras uden vrum bor garde?"]=1,
},
[267325]={ -- Walter Mason
  ["How can I help you?"]=1,
},
[267333]={ -- Terunne Bearshaper
  ["Care to learn how to gather leather from slain beasts? Or do you need some new tools?"]=1,
},
[267336]={ -- Brighid Stormflayer
  ["Care to learn how to gather leather from slain beasts? Or do you need some new tools?"]=1,
},
[267354]={ -- Black Skeletal Horse
  ["<It snaps its teeth together, chomping at its bit.>"]=1,
},
[267743]={ -- Projection of Periculus
  ["The Umbrawarden ignores your approach, staring off toward your camp."]=1,
},
[267786]={ -- Projection of Ignedus
  ["The Umbrawarden is intently examining the weaponry."]=1,
},
[267787]={ -- Projection of Gladius Reginax
  ["The Umbrawarden quickly stops talking and glares at you."]=1,
},
[267923]={ -- Custodian Veldharin
  ["Welcome to the Lycaneum! You stand in the presence of boundless knowledge and infinite magical potential! I, of course, mean the Sunstrider Omnium. I am but its mere keeper, here to answer and guide all young Magisters in their magical, academic journey. If you have any questions, you but simply have to ask."]=1,
  ["Well, when I insisted on asking a question, I meant about the Omnium, not about myself. But if you're so interested... I am Custodian Veldharin, appointed as Keeper of Knowledge by Grand Magister... er... who was it again? Grand Magister Mo--no, it wasn't her. Uh... well, regardless. Several Grand Magisters ago. I've clearly lost count. After the Second War, I was... encouraged to retire. Apparently, Anasterian wanted me to 'enjoy the many days I had remaining.' Which was his way of saying I was far too old for the position. So, I moved to live with my daughter, Elsharin. She served as a Seeker of Knowledge and Magisterial Ambassador to the Wizard's Sanctum in Stormwind."]=2,
  ["Of course I did and not just for the Omnium either! I lost two brothers and my dear sister when the city fell. All three of them were Magisters... I tried to assist the young prince in reviving... awakening? It was so... cold. But no matter what we tried, it simply... refused. Even with his key-cipher, it did not respond. After it was sealed away, I tried to help the surviving Magisters restore the Terrace... but they insisted I rest. And so I did, for a good many years. Some... not so good. But alas, I have returned and young Rommath was in no mood to try to stop me. Un-retirement is precisely what I needed after all these years!"]=3,
  ["I'd refer you to the plaque there on the Omnium. It summarizes Dath'Remar's intentions quite nicely. But in short, his reasons were many, his ambitions bold, and his purpose as clear as the skies over Eversong. Dath'Remar saw much in his youth and he dared not shy away from the magical forces of our world."]=4,
  ["An excellent question! Let's see... We have the Arcane Magicule, of course. Thousands of years of Highborne knowledge gave our fledgling people the resources to prosper in this new land. We have the fire and other elemental Magicules: the natural fundamentals of our very world. We have a curious collection of holy knowledge within the Light Magicule. The High Priests of Silvermoon did much to contribute to its knowledge. And, since everyone asks, there are the forbidden Magicules... Void. Fel. Necromancy... though I have to imagine that some of the restrictions on those may be... loosened. Veldharin's brow furrows in thought."]=5,
  ["Ah, yes. The Fel Magicule. A forbidden node of knowledge, at least it was. Fel was one of the first magics Dath'Remar credits as his catalyst for creating the Omnium. He saw its potential... and its horror during the days of the Highborne. He saw the creatures from beyond that wielded fel magic. When the time came, he saw the destructive truth of both fel and arcane in those final days of the War of the Ancients. Never again would he allow his people to be blindsided by such a destructive, unknown force. Over time, knowledge of fel and the Burning Legion was shared between the Magisters and the Council of Tirisfal. But beyond a select few, the Fel Magicule was forbidden to study. Oh, how times would change..."]=6,
  ["Narrows his glassy eyes. An... appropriate question, I suppose. It is--was--a fiercely forbidden node of knowledge, as decreed by Dath'Remar. When we first set upon the shores of Tirisfal, our ancestors encountered a darkness that clung to this land. The whispers drove many insane, feeding upon our paranoia, instigating fear and jealousy among our tired kin. Dath'Remar sought to understand where this magic came from and so he sent out the first of the Seekers. Few know what they found or encountered, but it was enough for Dath'Remar to stop its study. Only the most trusted and accomplished Magisters were permitted to plumb the knowledge within the Void Magicule."]=7,
},
[268174]={ -- Supplier Filmore
  ["Welcome to the Trading Post Inventory Clearance Extravaganza! We've gotta make space in our warehouses for all the new inventory coming in. So you're in luck, adventurer. We are going to pass some savings on to you."]=1,
